package com.rotitrack.app.data

// Generated from the "Roti Track Weight Loss Recipes" book. Edit the source JSON and regenerate.

private const val PART_1 = """[{"id":"r001","cat":"veg","title":"Creamy Dahi Baingan","intro":"Roasted brinjal slices simmered in a light, tangy curd gravy tempered with mustard seeds and curry leaves. Instead of deep-frying the brinjal, we roast it on a tawa with a few drops of oil, cutting the calories by more than half. The hung-curd base keeps it creamy without any cream. Perfect with a phulka for a filling, light lunch.","kcal":180,"protein":7,"minutes":30,"ingredients":["1 large brinjal, sliced into rounds","1 cup low-fat curd, whisked","1 tsp besan","1/2 tsp mustard seeds","8 curry leaves","1/2 tsp turmeric and 1 tsp red chilli powder","1 tsp oil","Salt and fresh coriander"],"steps":["Brush brinjal slices with a few drops of oil and roast on a hot tawa till soft and golden on both sides.","Whisk curd with besan, turmeric, chilli powder and salt until smooth.","Heat oil, crackle mustard seeds and curry leaves, then lower the flame.","Pour in the curd mixture and stir continuously for 3–4 minutes so it does not split.","Add the roasted brinjal, simmer for 2 minutes and garnish with coriander."],"benefits":["Brinjal is very low in calories and rich in fibre that keeps you full.","Curd provides probiotics and protein for better digestion.","Roasting instead of frying saves around 150 kcal per serving.","Mustard seeds and curry leaves support metabolism."]},{"id":"r002","cat":"veg","title":"Moong Dal Chilla","intro":"A protein-packed savoury pancake made from soaked yellow moong dal, ginger and green chillies. It is light on the stomach, cooks in minutes and keeps you satisfied until lunch. Stuff it with grated paneer or vegetables for an extra boost. One of the best Indian breakfasts for steady fat loss.","kcal":210,"protein":12,"minutes":25,"ingredients":["1 cup yellow moong dal, soaked 3 hours","1 inch ginger","2 green chillies","1/2 tsp cumin seeds","2 tbsp chopped coriander","1 small onion, finely chopped","1 tsp oil for the whole batch","Salt to taste"],"steps":["Drain the soaked dal and grind with ginger, chillies and a little water to a smooth batter.","Stir in cumin, onion, coriander and salt.","Heat a non-stick tawa and lightly grease with a few drops of oil.","Spread a ladle of batter into a thin round and cook on medium heat till edges lift.","Flip, cook the other side for a minute and serve hot with green chutney."],"benefits":["High in plant protein, which reduces hunger and cravings.","Low glycaemic index keeps blood sugar stable.","Easy to digest and gentle on the gut. Very little oil needed compared with","parathas."]},{"id":"r003","cat":"veg","title":"Lauki Chana Dal","intro":"A comforting home-style dal where bottle gourd and chana dal cook together into a thick, satisfying curry. Lauki adds bulk and water with almost no calories, while chana dal gives protein and slow-release energy. Tempered with jeera, hing and tomatoes, it tastes rich yet stays light. Great with brown rice or a jowar roti.","kcal":190,"protein":10,"minutes":35,"ingredients":["1/2 cup chana dal, soaked 1 hour","1 1/2 cups lauki, peeled and cubed","1 tomato, chopped","1/2 tsp turmeric","1 tsp cumin seeds and a pinch of hing","1 tsp ginger-garlic paste","1 tsp ghee","Salt and coriander"],"steps":["Pressure cook chana dal and lauki with turmeric, salt and 2 cups water for 3 whistles.","Heat ghee, add cumin seeds and hing, then ginger-garlic paste.","Add tomato and cook until soft and mushy.","Pour in the cooked dal and lauki, mash lightly and simmer 5 minutes.","Garnish with coriander and serve hot."],"benefits":["Lauki is 92% water and very low in calories.","Chana dal provides fibre and protein for long satiety.","Hing and cumin reduce bloating. A complete, balanced one-pot meal."]},{"id":"r004","cat":"veg","title":"Palak Paneer Without Cream","intro":"The restaurant classic made light: blanched spinach blended into a silky gravy and finished with soft cubes of low-fat paneer. We skip the cream and butter and use a spoon of curd for richness. It is loaded with iron, calcium and protein. One bowl keeps you full for hours.","kcal":260,"protein":18,"minutes":30,"ingredients":["2 bunches spinach, blanched","100 g low-fat paneer, cubed","1 onion, chopped","1 tomato, chopped","3 garlic cloves and 1 green chilli","1/2 tsp garam masala","2 tbsp low-fat curd","1 tsp oil and salt"],"steps":["Blanch spinach for 2 minutes, plunge in cold water and blend with chilli into a smooth puree.","Heat oil, saute garlic and onion till golden, then add tomato and cook soft.","Add the spinach puree, salt and garam masala and simmer 5 minutes.","Lower the heat, stir in whisked curd so it blends smoothly.","Add paneer cubes, simmer 2 minutes and serve."],"benefits":["Paneer protein preserves muscle while you lose fat.","Spinach is rich in iron and fibre with very few calories.","No cream means about 120 kcal less per serving.","Calcium helps support fat metabolism."]},{"id":"r005","cat":"veg","title":"Vegetable Oats Upma","intro":"A hearty South Indian style upma made with rolled oats instead of semolina. Colourful vegetables, mustard seeds and curry leaves give it a familiar taste with much more fibre. It cooks in under 20 minutes, making it ideal for busy mornings. A squeeze of lemon at the end brightens every bite.","kcal":230,"protein":8,"minutes":20,"ingredients":["1 cup rolled oats, dry-roasted","1/2 cup mixed carrot, beans and peas","1 small onion, chopped","1/2 tsp mustard seeds and 1 tsp urad dal","8 curry leaves and 1 green chilli","1 tsp oil","1 1/2 cups hot water","Salt and lemon juice"],"steps":["Dry-roast oats in a pan for 3 minutes and set aside.","Heat oil, add mustard seeds, urad dal, curry leaves and chilli.","Saute onion till soft, then add vegetables and cook 3 minutes.","Add salt and hot water, bring to a boil and stir in the oats.","Cook covered on low heat 3 minutes and finish with lemon juice."],"benefits":["Oats beta-glucan fibre keeps you full for longer.","Lower glycaemic load than rava upma.","Vegetables add vitamins and volume without calories.","Supports healthy cholesterol levels."]},{"id":"r006","cat":"veg","title":"Paneer Bhurji","intro":"Soft scrambled paneer cooked with onions, tomatoes and capsicum in a light spice mix. It is a vegetarian's answer to egg bhurji and is ready in 15 minutes. Use low-fat paneer and very little oil for a high-protein, low-carb meal. Wrap it in a lettuce leaf or enjoy with one multigrain roti.","kcal":240,"protein":19,"minutes":15,"ingredients":["150 g low-fat paneer, crumbled","1 onion, finely chopped","1 tomato, finely chopped","1/2 capsicum, chopped","1/4 tsp turmeric","1/2 tsp pav bhaji or garam masala","1 tsp oil","Salt and coriander"],"steps":["Heat oil, saute onion until translucent.","Add capsicum and tomato and cook until soft.","Add turmeric, masala and salt and cook 1 minute.","Stir in the crumbled paneer and mix well for 2 minutes.","Finish with coriander and serve hot."],"benefits":["Very high protein keeps hunger in control.","Low in carbohydrates, ideal for dinner.","Quick to cook so you avoid ordering out. Capsicum adds vitamin C and","antioxidants."]},{"id":"r007","cat":"veg","title":"Sprouts Chaat","intro":"A crunchy, tangy bowl of steamed mixed sprouts tossed with onion, tomato, cucumber, chaat masala and lemon. It satisfies the craving for street-style chaat with zero frying. Sprouting increases protein and makes nutrients easier to absorb. Perfect as an evening snack.","kcal":160,"protein":10,"minutes":10,"ingredients":["1 cup mixed sprouts (moong, chana, moth)","1 small onion, chopped","1 tomato, chopped","1/2 cucumber, chopped","1 green chilli, chopped","1 tsp chaat masala","Juice of 1 lemon","Coriander and salt"],"steps":["Steam the sprouts for 5 minutes so they stay crunchy.","Let them cool slightly in a large bowl.","Add onion, tomato, cucumber and chilli.","Sprinkle chaat masala and salt, squeeze lemon.","Toss with coriander and serve immediately."],"benefits":["Sprouts are rich in protein, fibre and enzymes.","Low calorie snack that replaces fried namkeen.","Vitamin C from lemon improves iron absorption.","Keeps you full until dinner."]},{"id":"r008","cat":"veg","title":"Lauki Kofta Curry (Baked)","intro":"Soft bottle-gourd koftas baked in the oven or air fryer instead of being deep-fried, then simmered in a tomato-onion gravy. You get all the indulgence of a festive kofta curry at a fraction of the calories. Besan binds the koftas and adds protein. Serve with a phulka for a special Sunday meal.","kcal":220,"protein":8,"minutes":40,"ingredients":["2 cups grated lauki, squeezed","4 tbsp besan","1/2 tsp each cumin and chilli powder","2 tomatoes and 1 onion, pureed","1 tsp ginger-garlic paste","1/2 tsp garam masala","1 tsp oil","Salt and coriander"],"steps":["Mix lauki, besan, cumin, chilli and salt and shape into small balls.","Bake at 200 C or air-fry for 15 minutes till golden, turning once.","Heat oil, cook ginger-garlic paste and onion-tomato puree until oil separates.","Add spices, salt and a cup of the saved lauki water and simmer 5 minutes.","Add koftas just before serving and garnish with coriander."],"benefits":["Baking saves about 200 kcal compared with frying.","Lauki is hydrating and very low in calories.","Besan adds plant protein and fibre. Tomato gravy gives lycopene and","antioxidants."]},{"id":"r009","cat":"veg","title":"Rajma Salad Bowl","intro":"Boiled kidney beans tossed with crunchy vegetables, mint and a lemony dressing. This bowl gives you all the goodness of rajma without the heavy gravy and rice. It is high in protein and fibre, making it a complete meal on its own. Pack it for office lunches.","kcal":250,"protein":13,"minutes":15,"ingredients":["1 cup boiled rajma","1/2 cucumber, diced","1 tomato, diced","1 small onion, diced","1/4 cup sweet corn (optional)","1 tsp roasted cumin powder","Juice of 1 lemon","Mint, coriander and salt"],"steps":["Rinse and drain the boiled rajma well.","Combine with cucumber, tomato, onion and corn in a bowl.","Add cumin powder, salt and lemon juice.","Toss with chopped mint and coriander.","Chill for 10 minutes before serving."],"benefits":["Rajma provides slow-digesting carbs and plant protein.","High fibre improves digestion and fullness.","No gravy or rice keeps calories low. Rich in iron and magnesium."]},{"id":"r010","cat":"veg","title":"Jowar Roti with Methi","intro":"Gluten-free sorghum rotis kneaded with fresh fenugreek leaves for a slightly bitter, earthy flavour. Jowar is a traditional millet that digests slowly and keeps blood sugar stable. Methi adds fibre and helps control appetite. Pair with dal or sabzi as a smart swap for wheat roti.","kcal":120,"protein":4,"minutes":20,"ingredients":["1 cup jowar flour","1/2 cup fresh methi leaves, chopped","1/2 tsp ajwain","1 green chilli, chopped","Warm water to knead","Salt to taste","A little dry flour for dusting"],"steps":["Mix jowar flour, methi, ajwain, chilli and salt.","Add warm water little by little and knead into a soft dough.","Pat each ball into a roti between your palms or on a sheet.","Cook on a hot tawa, sprinkle water on top and flip.","Roast directly on flame till it puffs and serve hot."],"benefits":["Gluten-free and rich in fibre. Millets have a lower glycaemic index","than wheat.","Methi helps reduce sugar cravings. No oil needed at all."]},{"id":"r011","cat":"veg","title":"Mixed Vegetable Soup","intro":"A warming, clear-style vegetable soup with carrots, beans, cabbage and tomato flavoured with garlic and black pepper. Having a bowl before meals is a proven way to eat fewer calories overall. It is light, hydrating and full of vitamins. Make a big pot and keep it ready for the week.","kcal":90,"protein":3,"minutes":20,"ingredients":["1 carrot, 6 beans and 1/2 cup cabbage, finely chopped","1 tomato, chopped","4 garlic cloves, minced","1 small onion, chopped","1 tsp oil","3 cups water","Black pepper and salt","Spring onion to garnish"],"steps":["Heat oil and saute garlic and onion for a minute.","Add all vegetables and tomato and stir-fry 3 minutes.","Pour water, add salt and simmer 10 minutes.","Mash a few vegetables to thicken the soup slightly.","Season generously with pepper and garnish with spring onion."],"benefits":["Very low calorie with high volume. Soup before a meal reduces total","intake.","Rich in vitamins A and C. Keeps you hydrated."]},{"id":"r012","cat":"veg","title":"Masala Oats","intro":"Savoury oats cooked with onion, tomato, peas and Indian spices into a soft, porridge-like dish. It is the healthier homemade version of the instant packets, without added sugar or preservatives. It keeps you full all morning. Add a spoon of curd on top for extra protein.","kcal":220,"protein":8,"minutes":15,"ingredients":["1 cup oats","1 small onion, chopped","1 tomato, chopped","1/4 cup green peas","1/4 tsp turmeric and 1/2 tsp garam masala","1 tsp oil","2 cups water","Salt and coriander"],"steps":["Heat oil, saute onion till soft.","Add tomato, peas, turmeric and masala and cook 3 minutes.","Add oats and stir for a minute.","Pour water and salt, cook on medium till thick and creamy.","Garnish with coriander and serve."],"benefits":["Soluble fibre controls appetite. No hidden sugar unlike instant","packets.","Steady energy release. Easy and quick to make."]},{"id":"r013","cat":"veg","title":"Besan Cheela with Veggies","intro":"Thin gram-flour pancakes loaded with grated vegetables and herbs. Besan is naturally high in protein and fibre, and the cheela needs just a few drops of oil. Make the batter in a few minutes and cook fresh. Delicious with mint chutney or a bowl of curd.","kcal":190,"protein":10,"minutes":15,"ingredients":["1/2 cup besan","1 small onion, finely chopped","1 small tomato, chopped","2 tbsp grated carrot","1 green chilli and coriander","1/4 tsp ajwain and turmeric","Water to make batter","1 tsp oil and salt"],"steps":["Whisk besan with water to a smooth, pourable batter.","Add vegetables, chilli, coriander, ajwain, turmeric and salt.","Heat a non-stick tawa and grease lightly.","Spread batter thinly and cook till the bottom is golden.","Flip, cook 1 minute and serve hot."],"benefits":["Gram flour is high in protein and fibre. Gluten-free and low glycaemic.","Vegetables add volume and nutrients. Great replacement for paratha","breakfasts."]},{"id":"r014","cat":"veg","title":"Cauliflower Rice Pulao","intro":"Grated cauliflower cooked like a fragrant pulao with whole spices, peas and carrots. It looks and tastes like rice but has about one-fifth of the carbohydrates. A smart dinner option when you are craving pulao. Serve with raita or dal.","kcal":140,"protein":5,"minutes":20,"ingredients":["1 small cauliflower, grated to rice size","1/4 cup green peas","1 carrot, finely diced","1 bay leaf, 2 cloves, 1 small cinnamon stick","1/2 tsp cumin seeds","1 green chilli, slit","1 tsp ghee","Salt and coriander"],"steps":["Grate the cauliflower and pat dry with a towel.","Heat ghee, add cumin and whole spices till fragrant.","Add chilli, peas and carrot and saute 3 minutes.","Add cauliflower rice and salt, stir-fry on high heat 4–5 minutes.","Fluff, garnish with coriander and serve."],"benefits":["Very low in carbs and calories. High fibre and vitamin C.","Satisfies rice cravings without spiking sugar.","Whole spices aid digestion."]},{"id":"r015","cat":"veg","title":"Tofu Tikka","intro":"Firm tofu cubes marinated in spiced hung curd and grilled with onion and capsicum. It has the smoky, tandoori flavour you love with lean plant protein. Bake, grill or air-fry. Serve as a starter or with salad for dinner.","kcal":200,"protein":16,"minutes":30,"ingredients":["200 g firm tofu, cubed","1/2 cup hung curd","1 tsp ginger-garlic paste","1 tsp kashmiri chilli powder","1/2 tsp garam masala and chaat masala","1 capsicum and 1 onion, cubed","1 tsp mustard oil","Salt and lemon juice"],"steps":["Press tofu to remove water, then cube.","Mix curd, ginger-garlic, spices, oil, salt and lemon.","Coat tofu and vegetables and marinate 20 minutes.","Thread on skewers and grill or air-fry at 200 C for 12 minutes.","Sprinkle chaat masala and serve."],"benefits":["Tofu is a complete plant protein. Low calorie, low carb starter.","Hung curd marinade adds probiotics. Grilling avoids extra oil."]},{"id":"r016","cat":"veg","title":"Palak Moong Dal","intro":"Yellow moong dal cooked with fresh spinach and finished with a garlic tadka. It is light, nourishing and full of protein and iron. The spinach melts into the dal giving it a beautiful green colour. Ideal for a light dinner.","kcal":180,"protein":11,"minutes":30,"ingredients":["1/2 cup yellow moong dal","2 cups spinach, chopped","1 tomato, chopped","1/4 tsp turmeric","4 garlic cloves, sliced","1/2 tsp cumin seeds","1 dry red chilli","1 tsp ghee and salt"],"steps":["Pressure cook dal with turmeric, tomato, salt and 2 cups water for 2 whistles.","Add spinach and simmer 4 minutes.","Heat ghee, add cumin, garlic and red chilli till golden.","Pour tadka over the dal.","Serve hot with rice or roti."],"benefits":["Moong dal is easy to digest. Spinach adds iron, folate and fibre.","Low fat, high protein dinner. Garlic supports metabolism."]},{"id":"r017","cat":"veg","title":"Bhindi Masala (Air Fried)","intro":"Crispy okra tossed with onions and tangy dry spices, made in the air fryer or on a tawa with minimal oil. The okra stays crisp and non-sticky. It is high in fibre and very low in calories. Serve with dal and a phulka.","kcal":130,"protein":4,"minutes":25,"ingredients":["250 g bhindi, washed, dried and sliced","1 onion, sliced","1/2 tsp turmeric","1 tsp coriander powder","1/2 tsp amchur powder","1/2 tsp red chilli powder","1 tsp oil","Salt"],"steps":["Dry the bhindi completely before slicing.","Toss with half the oil, turmeric and chilli and air-fry at 180 C for 12 minutes.","Saute onion in remaining oil till golden.","Add bhindi, coriander powder, amchur and salt.","Toss for 2 minutes and serve."],"benefits":["Bhindi is rich in soluble fibre. Helps regulate blood sugar.","Air frying uses 80% less oil. Supports gut health."]},{"id":"r018","cat":"veg","title":"Methi Thepla (Low Oil)","intro":"Soft Gujarati flatbreads made with whole wheat, besan, curd and fresh methi. These theplas use very little oil and stay fresh for travel. Besan and curd improve the protein content. Enjoy with curd or pickle-free chutney.","kcal":140,"protein":5,"minutes":25,"ingredients":["1 cup whole wheat flour","1/4 cup besan","1 cup methi leaves, chopped","2 tbsp curd","1/2 tsp each turmeric, chilli powder and ajwain","1 tsp ginger-chilli paste","1 tsp oil","Salt"],"steps":["Mix all ingredients and knead into a soft dough with water.","Rest for 10 minutes.","Roll into thin rounds.","Cook on a hot tawa with just a brush of oil.","Cook both sides till golden spots appear."],"benefits":["Methi fibre reduces appetite. Besan increases protein.","Low oil compared with parathas. Portable healthy meal."]},{"id":"r019","cat":"veg","title":"Soya Chunks Curry","intro":"Protein-rich soya chunks simmered in a spicy onion-tomato masala. Soya chunks have more protein than chicken by weight, making this a vegetarian power curry. It tastes meaty and satisfying. Serve with roti or brown rice.","kcal":230,"protein":22,"minutes":30,"ingredients":["1 cup soya chunks","1 onion, chopped","2 tomatoes, pureed","1 tsp ginger-garlic paste","1 tsp coriander powder and 1/2 tsp garam masala","1/2 tsp chilli powder and turmeric","1 tsp oil","Salt and coriander"],"steps":["Boil soya chunks in salted water 5 minutes, then squeeze dry.","Heat oil, saute onion and ginger-garlic till golden.","Add tomato puree and spices and cook till oil separates.","Add soya chunks and 1 cup water and simmer 8 minutes.","Garnish with coriander."],"benefits":["Very high plant protein. Low fat and cholesterol free.","Keeps you full for hours. Budget-friendly protein source."]},{"id":"r020","cat":"veg","title":"Vegetable Dalia","intro":"Broken wheat cooked with mixed vegetables into a soft, savoury khichdi-style meal. Dalia is a whole grain full of fibre, and it cooks quickly in a pressure cooker. It is filling and easy to digest. Perfect for breakfast or dinner.","kcal":240,"protein":8,"minutes":25,"ingredients":["1/2 cup dalia (broken wheat)","1/2 cup mixed vegetables","1 small onion, chopped","1/2 tsp cumin seeds","1/4 tsp turmeric","1 green chilli","1 tsp ghee","2 cups water and salt"],"steps":["Dry-roast dalia for 3 minutes.","Heat ghee, add cumin, onion and chilli.","Add vegetables and saute 2 minutes.","Add dalia, turmeric, salt and water.","Pressure cook 2 whistles and serve hot."],"benefits":["Whole grain with high fibre. Slow digestion keeps you full.","Light on the stomach. Rich in B vitamins."]},{"id":"r021","cat":"veg","title":"Paneer Tikka","intro":"Chunks of paneer and vegetables marinated in spiced curd and grilled until charred. This classic starter is naturally high in protein and low in carbohydrates. Using low-fat paneer and grilling keeps it light. Serve with mint chutney.","kcal":250,"protein":20,"minutes":30,"ingredients":["200 g low-fat paneer, cubed","1/2 cup hung curd","1 tsp ginger-garlic paste","1 tsp kashmiri chilli","1/2 tsp garam masala","1 onion and 1 capsicum, cubed","1 tsp mustard oil","Salt and lemon"],"steps":["Whisk curd with spices, oil, salt and lemon.","Coat paneer and vegetables and rest 20 minutes.","Thread on skewers.","Grill or air-fry at 200 C for 10–12 minutes.","Serve with chutney and onion rings."],"benefits":["High protein snack. Low carb.","Curd adds probiotics. No deep frying."]},{"id":"r022","cat":"veg","title":"Lauki Raita","intro":"A cool, soothing raita of whisked curd and lightly cooked grated bottle gourd, seasoned with roasted cumin and fresh mint. It balances spicy curries and calms the stomach on hot days. With very few calories and a good dose of probiotics, it is a smart side for every meal. Make it fresh and serve chilled.","kcal":80,"protein":5,"minutes":10,"ingredients":["1/2 cup grated lauki","1 cup low-fat curd","1/2 tsp roasted cumin powder","Pinch of black salt","1 tbsp chopped mint","1 green chilli, finely chopped (optional)","Pinch of red chilli powder","Salt to taste"],"steps":["Boil the grated lauki in a little water for 2 minutes, squeeze out the water and let it cool.","Whisk the curd until smooth and creamy.","Fold in the cooled lauki, chilli, cumin, black salt and salt.","Stir in the chopped mint.","Sprinkle red chilli powder on top, chill for 15 minutes and serve."],"benefits":["Cooling and very hydrating. Probiotic curd supports gut health.","Under 100 kcal per bowl. Helps digestion after heavy meals."]},{"id":"r023","cat":"veg","title":"Quinoa Vegetable Khichdi","intro":"A wholesome one-pot khichdi made with quinoa and moong dal instead of rice. Quinoa is a complete protein and has more fibre than white rice. It is comforting, light and easy to digest. Serve with curd or kadhi.","kcal":260,"protein":10,"minutes":25,"ingredients":["1/2 cup quinoa, washed","1/4 cup yellow moong dal","1/2 cup mixed vegetables","1/2 tsp cumin seeds","1/4 tsp turmeric","1 tsp ginger, grated","1 tsp ghee","3 cups water and salt"],"steps":["Rinse quinoa and dal well.","Heat ghee, add cumin and ginger.","Add vegetables and saute 2 minutes.","Add quinoa, dal, turmeric, salt and water.","Pressure cook 2 whistles and serve."],"benefits":["Complete plant protein. High fibre and minerals.","Gluten-free. Comforting light dinner."]},{"id":"r024","cat":"veg","title":"Mushroom Matar","intro":"Button mushrooms and sweet green peas simmered in a spiced onion-tomato gravy. Mushrooms are extremely low in calories yet give a meaty, satisfying bite, while peas add plant protein and fibre. This curry comes together in under half an hour, making it perfect for weeknights. Serve with phulka or millet roti.","kcal":170,"protein":8,"minutes":25,"ingredients":["200 g button mushrooms, sliced","1/2 cup green peas","1 onion, finely chopped","2 tomatoes, pureed","1 tsp ginger-garlic paste","1 tsp coriander powder and 1/2 tsp garam masala","1/4 tsp turmeric and 1/2 tsp chilli powder","1 tsp oil, salt and coriander"],"steps":["Heat oil and saute onion until golden, then add ginger-garlic paste for a minute.","Pour in tomato puree with turmeric, chilli and coriander powder and cook till oil separates.","Add mushrooms and peas and stir well to coat with the masala.","Add 1/2 cup water and salt, cover and cook 8 minutes.","Finish with garam masala and fresh coriander."],"benefits":["Mushrooms are very low in calories. Rich in B vitamins and vitamin D.","Peas add protein and fibre. Satisfying curry with minimal oil."]},{"id":"r025","cat":"veg","title":"Ragi Dosa","intro":"A crisp, instant dosa made from finger millet flour, rice flour and curd. Ragi is rich in calcium and fibre and helps keep you full. No fermentation is needed. Serve with coconut-free green chutney or sambar.","kcal":150,"protein":5,"minutes":20,"ingredients":["1 cup ragi flour","2 tbsp rice flour","2 tbsp curd","1 small onion, chopped","1 green chilli and coriander","1/2 tsp cumin seeds","Water as needed","Salt and a few drops oil"],"steps":["Mix flours, curd, salt and water into a thin batter.","Add onion, chilli, cumin and coriander.","Pour onto a hot tawa from the outer edge inward.","Drizzle a few drops of oil.","Cook till crisp and fold."],"benefits":["Ragi is high in calcium and fibre. Low glycaemic index.","Gluten-free option. Keeps hunger away."]},{"id":"r026","cat":"veg","title":"Chana Masala (Light)","intro":"Chickpeas simmered in a tangy, spicy masala made with very little oil. Chickpeas give you both protein and fibre so one bowl is very satisfying. Add tea-bag water for the dark colour without extra oil. Serve with salad.","kcal":240,"protein":12,"minutes":30,"ingredients":["1 cup boiled chickpeas","1 onion, chopped","2 tomatoes, pureed","1 tsp ginger-garlic paste","1 tsp chana masala","1/2 tsp amchur","1 tsp oil","Salt and coriander"],"steps":["Heat oil, saute onion and ginger-garlic.","Add tomato puree and cook till thick.","Add chana masala, amchur and salt.","Add chickpeas and 1 cup water and simmer 10 minutes.","Mash a few chickpeas, garnish and serve."],"benefits":["High fibre and plant protein. Slow carbs.","Low oil. Keeps you full."]},{"id":"r027","cat":"veg","title":"Stuffed Capsicum","intro":"Colourful bell peppers filled with a spiced paneer and vegetable stuffing and roasted until tender and slightly charred. It looks impressive on the table yet is very light on calories. The paneer filling gives protein, while capsicum adds crunch and vitamin C. A lovely dinner when guests come over.","kcal":180,"protein":12,"minutes":35,"ingredients":["3 capsicums, tops cut and seeds removed","100 g low-fat paneer, crumbled","1 small boiled potato or 1/2 cup boiled peas","1 onion, finely chopped","1/2 tsp garam masala","1/2 tsp chaat masala","1 tsp oil","Salt and coriander"],"steps":["Heat half the oil, saute onion till soft, then add potato or peas, paneer, spices and salt.","Mix in coriander and let the filling cool slightly.","Stuff the filling firmly into each capsicum and replace the tops.","Brush the outside with the remaining oil.","Bake at 200 C for 20 minutes or cook covered in a pan, turning, until tender."],"benefits":["Capsicum is loaded with vitamin C. Paneer adds lean protein.","Baked, not fried. Low-calorie, high-volume dinner."]},{"id":"r028","cat":"veg","title":"Cabbage Peas Sabzi","intro":"A simple, everyday dry sabzi of shredded cabbage and green peas tempered with mustard seeds, green chilli and turmeric. It is one of the lowest-calorie vegetable dishes you can cook, yet very filling. Cabbage is excellent for gut health. Ready in 20 minutes with just one teaspoon of oil.","kcal":110,"protein":4,"minutes":20,"ingredients":["3 cups cabbage, finely shredded","1/2 cup green peas","1 green chilli, chopped","1/2 tsp mustard seeds","1/2 tsp cumin seeds","1/4 tsp turmeric","1 tsp oil","Salt and coriander"],"steps":["Heat oil and crackle mustard and cumin seeds.","Add green chilli and peas and saute 2 minutes.","Add cabbage, turmeric and salt and mix well.","Cook uncovered on medium heat, stirring, until tender-crisp, about 8 minutes.","Garnish with coriander and serve with roti or dal."],"benefits":["Extremely low in calories. High fibre supports digestion.","Rich in vitamins C and K. Peas add a little protein."]},{"id":"r029","cat":"veg","title":"Moong Sprouts Dosa (Pesarattu)","intro":"A n Andhra classic: a thin, crisp dosa made from whole green moong ground with ginger and green chillies, with no rice at all. It is naturally high in protein and fibre and very satisfying. Topped with chopped onions, it is traditionally served with ginger chutney. A brilliant weight-loss breakfast.","kcal":170,"protein":11,"minutes":20,"ingredients":["1 cup whole green moong, soaked overnight","1 inch ginger","2 green chillies","1/2 tsp cumin seeds","1 onion, finely chopped","2 tbsp coriander","Salt to taste","Few drops oil"],"steps":["Drain moong and grind with ginger, chillies, cumin and a little water to a smooth batter.","Add salt; the batter should be pourable but not runny.","Pour a ladle on a hot tawa and spread thinly in circles.","Sprinkle onion and coriander and drizzle a few drops of oil.","Cook till crisp and golden, fold and serve hot."],"benefits":["Protein-rich breakfast with no rice. High fibre and low glycaemic.","No fermentation needed. Keeps you full till lunch."]},{"id":"r030","cat":"veg","title":"Kala Chana Chaat","intro":"A tangy, spicy chaat of boiled black chickpeas tossed with onion, tomato, green chilli, lemon and chaat masala. Kala chana is rich in protein, iron and fibre and keeps hunger away for hours. It is a perfect evening snack or pre-workout bite. Boil a batch and enjoy it through the week.","kcal":180,"protein":10,"minutes":10,"ingredients":["1 cup kala chana, soaked overnight and boiled","1 onion, finely chopped","1 tomato, finely chopped","1 green chilli, chopped","1 tsp chaat masala","1/2 tsp roasted cumin powder","Juice of 1 lemon","Coriander and salt"],"steps":["Drain the boiled chana and let it cool slightly.","Add onion, tomato and green chilli.","Sprinkle chaat masala, cumin powder and salt.","Squeeze lemon juice and toss well.","Garnish with coriander and serve."],"benefits":["High in protein and iron. Low glycaemic snack.","Fibre keeps you full. A smart swap for fried namkeen."]},{"id":"r031","cat":"veg","title":"Lauki Dosa","intro":"A n instant, soft dosa made by blending raw bottle gourd with rice flour, rava and curd. Lauki adds moisture and volume so each dosa has fewer calories than a regular one. No soaking or fermenting is needed, so it is ready in minutes. Kids love it too.","kcal":140,"protein":5,"minutes":20,"ingredients":["1 cup lauki, peeled and chopped","1/2 cup rice flour","2 tbsp fine rava","2 tbsp curd","1 green chilli and small piece ginger","1/2 tsp cumin seeds","Salt to taste","Few drops of oil"],"steps":["Blend lauki, chilli and ginger to a smooth puree without water.","Mix with rice flour, rava, curd, cumin and salt into a pourable batter.","Rest for 10 minutes.","Spread on a hot greased tawa and drizzle a few drops of oil.","Cook till golden and crisp, fold and serve with chutney."],"benefits":["Lauki is hydrating and very low in calories.","Fewer carbs than a regular dosa.","Light and easy to digest. Sneaks vegetables into breakfast."]},{"id":"r032","cat":"veg","title":"Kadhi Without Pakora","intro":"A light Punjabi-style kadhi made from curd and besan, tempered with methi seeds and curry leaves. We skip the fried pakoras and add boiled vegetables or sprouts instead. The tangy, warming flavour makes it a comforting meal with brown rice. Probiotic curd makes it gut-friendly.","kcal":120,"protein":6,"minutes":25,"ingredients":["1 cup low-fat curd","2 tbsp besan","2 cups water","1/4 tsp turmeric","1/2 tsp methi seeds and 1/2 tsp cumin","8 curry leaves and 1 dry red chilli","1 tsp ghee","Salt"],"steps":["Whisk curd, besan, turmeric, salt and water until lump-free.","Bring to a boil while stirring, then simmer 15 minutes.","Heat ghee, add methi seeds, cumin, red chilli and curry leaves.","Pour the tadka into the kadhi.","Serve hot with brown rice or millet."],"benefits":["Probiotics support digestion. No fried pakoras saves around 200","kcal.","Besan adds protein. Methi seeds help control blood sugar."]},{"id":"r033","cat":"veg","title":"Baingan Bharta","intro":"Smoky fire-roasted brinjal mashed and cooked with onion, tomato, garlic and green chillies. The charred flavour makes it taste rich even with just a teaspoon of oil. Brinjal is naturally low in calories and high in fibre. Serve with jowar or bajra roti.","kcal":120,"protein":3,"minutes":30,"ingredients":["1 large brinjal","1 onion, chopped","2 tomatoes, chopped","4 garlic cloves","1 green chilli","1/2 tsp red chilli powder","1 tsp mustard oil","Salt and coriander"],"steps":["Roast the brinjal directly on flame until the skin is charred and the inside is soft.","Cool, peel and mash the pulp.","Heat oil, saute garlic, chilli and onion till golden.","Add tomatoes and spices and cook till soft.","Add mashed brinjal, cook 5 minutes and garnish."],"benefits":["Very low calorie vegetable. Fibre keeps you full.","Rich in antioxidants. Smoky taste with almost no oil."]},{"id":"r034","cat":"veg","title":"Paneer Salad Bowl","intro":"A crunchy bowl of grilled paneer cubes, cucumber, cherry tomatoes, capsicum and lettuce tossed in a mint-lemon dressing. It is high in protein and very quick to assemble. Great for lunch boxes. Add roasted seeds for crunch.","kcal":230,"protein":18,"minutes":10,"ingredients":["100 g low-fat paneer, cubed and grilled","1 cucumber, chopped","6 cherry tomatoes, halved","1/2 capsicum, chopped","Handful lettuce","1 tsp roasted seeds","Lemon juice and mint","Salt, pepper and chaat masala"],"steps":["Grill paneer cubes on a hot pan with a pinch of salt and pepper.","Chop all vegetables into bite-size pieces.","Whisk lemon juice, chopped mint, salt and chaat masala.","Toss vegetables and paneer with dressing.","Top with roasted seeds and serve."],"benefits":["High protein, low carb meal. Raw vegetables give vitamins and fibre.","No heavy dressing. Keeps you energetic."]},{"id":"r035","cat":"veg","title":"Methi Matar Malai (Light)","intro":"Fresh fenugreek and green peas in a creamy white gravy made with cashew-free, curd and onion base. It tastes festive but stays light. Methi helps with appetite control. Pair with phulka.","kcal":190,"protein":8,"minutes":30,"ingredients":["2 cups methi leaves","1 cup green peas","1 onion, boiled and pureed","1/2 cup low-fat milk","2 tbsp curd","1/2 tsp garam masala","1 tsp oil","Salt"],"steps":["Saute methi in oil for 3 minutes until wilted.","Add onion puree and cook 3 minutes.","Add peas, milk and salt and simmer 5 minutes.","Lower the flame and stir in curd and garam masala.","Serve hot."],"benefits":["Methi reduces cravings. Peas add protein.","Light creamy taste without cream. Rich in fibre."]},{"id":"r036","cat":"veg","title":"Hara Bhara Kabab (Baked)","intro":"Green kebabs made with spinach, peas and a little potato, baked or air-fried till crisp. A great party starter without deep frying. Roasted besan binds them and adds protein. Serve with green chutney.","kcal":160,"protein":7,"minutes":35,"ingredients":["1 cup spinach, blanched","1/2 cup peas, boiled","1 small potato, boiled","3 tbsp roasted besan","1 green chilli and ginger","1/2 tsp chaat masala","1 tsp oil","Salt"],"steps":["Chop spinach finely and mash with peas and potato.","Add besan, chilli, ginger, chaat masala and salt.","Shape into small flat kebabs.","Brush with oil and bake at 200 C for 20 minutes.","Serve with chutney."],"benefits":["Baked, not fried. Loaded with greens.","Good fibre and iron. Healthy party snack."]},{"id":"r037","cat":"veg","title":"Ragi Idli","intro":"Soft, earthy steamed idlis made with finger millet flour, rava and curd. Because they are steamed, they need zero oil, and ragi adds plenty of calcium and fibre. No overnight fermentation is required, so you can make them any morning. Serve with sambar and green chutney.","kcal":130,"protein":5,"minutes":25,"ingredients":["1/2 cup ragi flour","1/2 cup fine rava","1 cup curd","1 tbsp grated carrot","1/2 tsp eno fruit salt","1/2 tsp mustard seeds and 6 curry leaves (optional tempering)","Salt","Water as needed"],"steps":["Mix ragi, rava, curd, carrot and salt with water into a thick batter.","Rest the batter for 15 minutes.","Add an optional mustard-curry leaf tempering to the batter.","Just before steaming, add eno and mix gently.","Pour into greased idli moulds and steam for 12 minutes."],"benefits":["Completely oil-free. Rich in calcium.","Low glycaemic index. Filling, light breakfast."]},{"id":"r038","cat":"veg","title":"Vegetable Sambar","intro":"A tangy toor dal and vegetable stew flavoured with tamarind and sambar powder. Loaded with drumstick, pumpkin, brinjal and carrots, it is high in fibre and protein. A big bowl is very satisfying. Serve with idli or millet.","kcal":150,"protein":7,"minutes":35,"ingredients":["1/2 cup toor dal","1 1/2 cups mixed vegetables","1 tbsp tamarind pulp","1 1/2 tsp sambar powder","1/2 tsp mustard seeds","8 curry leaves","1 tsp oil","Salt and hing"],"steps":["Pressure cook dal till soft and mash.","Boil vegetables with tamarind, sambar powder and salt.","Add dal and simmer 10 minutes.","Temper mustard, curry leaves and hing in oil.","Pour over sambar and serve."],"benefits":["Protein and fibre together. Lots of vegetables.","Low fat. Good for digestion."]},{"id":"r039","cat":"veg","title":"Corn Spinach Sandwich (Open)","intro":"A n open toast on multigrain bread topped with spinach, sweet corn and a little cheese, grilled till bubbly. It satisfies junk-food cravings with real nutrition. Use 1 slice per serving. Quick breakfast or snack.","kcal":220,"protein":10,"minutes":15,"ingredients":["2 slices multigrain bread","1/2 cup spinach, chopped","1/4 cup sweet corn","2 tbsp hung curd","1 tbsp grated cheese","1/4 tsp oregano and chilli flakes","Pepper and salt"],"steps":["Saute spinach and corn for 2 minutes.","Mix with hung curd, salt, pepper and herbs.","Spread over bread slices.","Top with a little cheese.","Bake or toast covered till cheese melts."],"benefits":["Whole grain bread adds fibre. Spinach adds iron.","Portion-controlled snack. Hung curd replaces mayo."]}]"""

private const val PART_2 = """[{"id":"r040","cat":"veg","title":"Masoor Dal Tadka","intro":"Red lentils cooked quickly and finished with a fragrant garlic-tomato tadka. Masoor dal cooks without soaking and is rich in protein. It is a staple comfort food that suits weight loss. Serve with rice or roti.","kcal":180,"protein":11,"minutes":25,"ingredients":["1/2 cup masoor dal","1 tomato, chopped","1/4 tsp turmeric","4 garlic cloves","1/2 tsp cumin","1 dry red chilli","1 tsp ghee","Salt and coriander"],"steps":["Wash dal and cook with turmeric, salt and 2 cups water till soft.","Heat ghee, add cumin, garlic and red chilli.","Add tomato and cook soft.","Pour tadka into dal and simmer 2 minutes.","Garnish and serve."],"benefits":["High protein lentil. Quick to cook.","Rich in folate and iron. Low fat."]},{"id":"r041","cat":"veg","title":"Tinda Masala","intro":"Tender round gourds cooked in a light, homestyle onion-tomato masala. Tinda is one of the lightest vegetables in the Indian kitchen, full of water and fibre. It soaks up the spices beautifully and stays soft. A gentle, summer-friendly sabzi that pairs well with phulka and dal.","kcal":110,"protein":3,"minutes":25,"ingredients":["4 tinda, peeled and quartered","1 onion, finely chopped","1 tomato, chopped","1/2 tsp cumin seeds","1/4 tsp turmeric","1 tsp coriander powder","1/2 tsp red chilli powder","1 tsp oil, salt and coriander"],"steps":["Heat oil, add cumin seeds and saute onion till soft.","Add tomato and all spices and cook until mushy.","Add tinda and salt and stir to coat.","Add 1/4 cup water, cover and cook 12–15 minutes till tender.","Garnish with coriander and serve."],"benefits":["Very low in calories. Hydrating and cooling.","Gentle on digestion. High fibre."]},{"id":"r042","cat":"veg","title":"Chickpea Salad","intro":"A bright, Mediterranean-style salad of chickpeas, cucumber, tomato, onion and fresh herbs dressed with lemon and a teaspoon of olive oil. It is a complete meal in a bowl with protein, fibre and healthy fats. It keeps well in the fridge for two days. Great for office lunches.","kcal":230,"protein":11,"minutes":10,"ingredients":["1 cup boiled chickpeas","1 cucumber, diced","1 tomato, diced","1 small onion, diced","1 tsp olive oil","Juice of 1 lemon","2 tbsp chopped mint and parsley or coriander","Salt, pepper and roasted cumin"],"steps":["Rinse and drain the chickpeas well.","Combine chickpeas, cucumber, tomato and onion in a bowl.","Whisk olive oil, lemon, salt, pepper and cumin.","Pour the dressing over and toss.","Add herbs, chill 10 minutes and serve."],"benefits":["Plant protein and fibre in one bowl. Healthy fats from olive oil.","Make-ahead meal. Keeps you full for hours."]},{"id":"r043","cat":"veg","title":"Dudhi Thalipeeth","intro":"A Maharashtrian multigrain flatbread made with jowar, bajra and besan mixed with grated bottle gourd, onion and spices. The lauki gives moisture so no extra water is needed. It is crisp outside, soft inside and needs very little oil. Enjoy with a bowl of curd.","kcal":150,"protein":6,"minutes":25,"ingredients":["1 cup mixed flour (jowar, bajra, besan)","1 cup grated lauki","1 onion, finely chopped","1/2 tsp cumin seeds","1 green chilli, chopped","2 tbsp coriander","1 tsp oil","Salt"],"steps":["Combine flours, lauki, onion, cumin, chilli, coriander and salt, knead without water.","Divide into balls.","Pat each ball into a thin round on a greased sheet with wet fingers.","Make 3–4 holes in the centre and transfer to a hot tawa.","Drizzle a few drops of oil in the holes, cook both sides till crisp."],"benefits":["Multigrain fibre. Lauki adds volume with few calories.","Gluten-free option. Very little oil needed."]},{"id":"r044","cat":"veg","title":"Broccoli Paneer Stir Fry","intro":"Broccoli florets, capsicum and paneer cubes tossed on high heat with garlic, soy sauce and black pepper. It is a quick Indo-Chinese style dish that is high in protein and low in carbohydrates. The vegetables stay crisp and colourful. A perfect 15-minute dinner.","kcal":200,"protein":16,"minutes":15,"ingredients":["1 cup broccoli florets","100 g low-fat paneer, cubed","1/2 capsicum, cubed","1 small onion, cubed","4 garlic cloves, chopped","1 tsp light soy sauce","1/2 tsp black pepper","1 tsp oil and salt"],"steps":["Blanch broccoli in boiling water for 2 minutes and drain.","Heat oil on high and saute garlic for 30 seconds.","Add onion, capsicum and broccoli and toss for 2 minutes.","Add paneer, soy sauce, pepper and salt.","Toss for 2 more minutes and serve hot."],"benefits":["High protein, low carb meal. Broccoli is rich in fibre and vitamin C.","Ready in 15 minutes. Minimal oil."]},{"id":"r045","cat":"veg","title":"Mixed Dal Khichdi","intro":"A comforting one-pot khichdi made with brown rice and a mix of moong, masoor and toor dal. The dal-to-rice ratio is higher than usual, making it richer in protein. It is easy to digest and wonderfully soothing. Serve with curd and a simple salad.","kcal":260,"protein":10,"minutes":25,"ingredients":["1/4 cup brown rice","1/4 cup mixed dal (moong, masoor, toor)","1/2 tsp cumin seeds","1/4 tsp turmeric","1 tsp grated ginger","Pinch of hing","1 tsp ghee","3 cups water and salt"],"steps":["Wash rice and dal and soak for 20 minutes.","Heat ghee, add cumin, hing and ginger.","Add rice, dal, turmeric, salt and water.","Pressure cook for 4 whistles.","Mash lightly and serve hot."],"benefits":["Complete protein from dal and rice. Easy to digest.","Brown rice adds fibre. Light, comforting dinner."]},{"id":"r046","cat":"veg","title":"Cucumber Peanut Salad (Koshimbir)","intro":"A crunchy Maharashtrian salad of finely chopped cucumber with crushed roasted peanuts, green chilli, lemon and a cumin tempering. It is refreshing, light and adds texture to any meal. Peanuts add healthy fats and a little protein. Ready in ten minutes.","kcal":120,"protein":4,"minutes":10,"ingredients":["2 cucumbers, finely chopped","2 tbsp roasted peanuts, coarsely crushed","1 green chilli, finely chopped","Juice of 1/2 lemon","1/2 tsp cumin seeds","1/2 tsp ghee or oil","2 tbsp coriander","Salt"],"steps":["Place cucumber in a bowl and gently squeeze out extra water.","Add peanuts, chilli, salt and lemon juice.","Heat ghee and crackle cumin seeds.","Pour the tempering over the salad.","Mix, garnish with coriander and serve fresh."],"benefits":["Very hydrating. Healthy fats from peanuts.","Low calorie crunch. Supports digestion."]},{"id":"r047","cat":"veg","title":"Aloo-Free Vegetable Cutlet","intro":"Crispy vegetable cutlets bound with oats and besan instead of potato. They are loaded with carrots, beans and peas and pan-roasted in very little oil. The oats add fibre and keep the cutlets light. Serve as an evening snack with green chutney.","kcal":140,"protein":6,"minutes":30,"ingredients":["1/2 cup oats, powdered","1 cup carrot, beans and peas, boiled and mashed","2 tbsp besan","1/2 tsp garam masala","1/2 tsp chaat masala","1 green chilli and 2 tbsp coriander","1 tsp oil","Salt"],"steps":["Mash the boiled vegetables well.","Add oats, besan, spices, chilli, coriander and salt.","Mix into a firm dough and shape into flat cutlets.","Heat a non-stick pan and brush with oil.","Pan-roast cutlets 3–4 minutes per side until golden."],"benefits":["No potato means fewer carbs. Oats add fibre.","Pan-roasted, not fried. Kid-friendly snack."]},{"id":"r048","cat":"veg","title":"Bajra Khichdi","intro":"A rustic Rajasthani khichdi of pearl millet and yellow moong dal finished with a ghee-hing tempering. Bajra is warming, rich in iron and keeps you full for a long time. It is a traditional winter comfort food. Serve with curd and a green salad.","kcal":250,"protein":9,"minutes":35,"ingredients":["1/4 cup whole bajra, soaked overnight","1/4 cup yellow moong dal","1/2 tsp cumin seeds","Pinch of hing","1/4 tsp turmeric","1 tsp ghee","3 cups water","Salt"],"steps":["Drain the soaked bajra and lightly pound it.","Pressure cook bajra with water and salt for 5 whistles.","Add moong dal and turmeric and cook 2 more whistles.","Heat ghee, add cumin and hing.","Pour the tempering over the khichdi and serve."],"benefits":["Rich in iron and magnesium. High-fibre millet.","Low glycaemic index. Warming winter meal."]},{"id":"r049","cat":"veg","title":"Green Moong Curry","intro":"Whole green moong simmered in a light onion-tomato gravy with ginger and garlic. It is a wholesome, protein-rich curry that is easy to digest. Whole moong keeps you full and steadies blood sugar. Serve with a phulka or a small bowl of brown rice.","kcal":210,"protein":13,"minutes":35,"ingredients":["1/2 cup whole green moong, soaked 4 hours","1 onion, chopped","1 tomato, chopped","1 tsp ginger-garlic paste","1/2 tsp cumin seeds","1 tsp coriander powder and 1/2 tsp garam masala","1 tsp oil","Salt and coriander"],"steps":["Pressure cook moong with salt, turmeric and 2 cups water for 3 whistles.","Heat oil, add cumin and saute onion and ginger-garlic.","Add tomato and spices and cook to a soft masala.","Add the cooked moong and simmer 8 minutes.","Garnish with coriander."],"benefits":["High plant protein. Rich in fibre.","Low fat. Gentle on digestion."]},{"id":"r050","cat":"veg","title":"Pumpkin Soup","intro":"A velvety, golden soup of pumpkin cooked with onion and garlic and finished with black pepper. Blending makes it creamy without any cream. Pumpkin is low in calories and rich in beta-carotene. Garnish with roasted pumpkin seeds for crunch.","kcal":100,"protein":3,"minutes":25,"ingredients":["2 cups yellow pumpkin, cubed","1 onion, chopped","3 garlic cloves","1 tsp oil","2 cups water","1/2 tsp black pepper","Salt","1 tsp roasted pumpkin seeds"],"steps":["Heat oil and saute onion and garlic for 2 minutes.","Add pumpkin, water and salt and cook covered until soft.","Cool slightly and blend until smooth.","Reheat, adjust thickness and add pepper.","Garnish with pumpkin seeds and serve."],"benefits":["Low calorie and filling. Rich in vitamin A.","Creamy without cream. Comforting starter."]},{"id":"r051","cat":"veg","title":"Rajma Masala (Light)","intro":"Kidney beans simmered in a thick, aromatic onion-tomato gravy using just one teaspoon of oil. It is the weekend favourite made weight-loss friendly. Eat it with half your usual rice and a big salad. Rich in plant protein and fibre.","kcal":250,"protein":13,"minutes":40,"ingredients":["1 cup boiled rajma","1 onion, finely chopped","2 tomatoes, pureed","1 tsp ginger-garlic paste","1 tsp rajma masala","1/2 tsp cumin seeds","1 tsp oil","Salt and coriander"],"steps":["Heat oil, add cumin and saute onion till golden.","Add ginger-garlic and tomato puree and cook till thick.","Add rajma masala and salt.","Add rajma and 1 cup water and simmer 15 minutes.","Mash a few beans to thicken and garnish."],"benefits":["Plant protein and fibre. Slow-digesting carbs.","Low oil gravy. Very filling."]},{"id":"r052","cat":"veg","title":"Karela Fry (Air Fried)","intro":"Thin bitter gourd rings coated in spices and a little besan, then air-fried until crisp. Salting first reduces the bitterness, and the crunch makes them addictive. Karela is famous for helping manage blood sugar. Serve as a side with dal and rice.","kcal":90,"protein":2,"minutes":25,"ingredients":["2 karela, thinly sliced","1/2 tsp turmeric","1 tsp red chilli powder","1 tsp besan","1/2 tsp amchur powder","1/2 tsp chaat masala","1 tsp oil","Salt"],"steps":["Rub karela slices with salt and rest 15 minutes, then squeeze out the juice.","Toss with turmeric, chilli, amchur and besan.","Drizzle oil and mix to coat.","Air-fry at 180 C for 12 minutes, shaking halfway.","Sprinkle chaat masala and serve."],"benefits":["Helps control blood sugar. Very low in calories.","Crunchy without deep frying. Rich in antioxidants."]},{"id":"r053","cat":"veg","title":"Paneer Stuffed Chilla","intro":"A thin besan chilla folded over a spiced crumbled paneer filling. This double-protein breakfast keeps you full till lunch. The batter takes five minutes and the chilla cooks in two. Serve with green chutney.","kcal":260,"protein":20,"minutes":20,"ingredients":["1/2 cup besan","50 g low-fat paneer, crumbled","1 small onion, finely chopped","1 green chilli, chopped","2 tbsp coriander","1/4 tsp ajwain and turmeric","1/2 tsp chaat masala","Salt and few drops oil"],"steps":["Whisk besan with water, ajwain, turmeric and salt into a smooth batter.","Mix paneer with onion, chilli, coriander and chaat masala.","Spread batter thinly on a hot greased tawa.","Spoon the filling onto one half once the top sets.","Fold, cook 1 minute per side and serve."],"benefits":["Over 20 g protein. Low carb breakfast.","Keeps you full for hours. Ready in 20 minutes."]},{"id":"r054","cat":"veg","title":"Veg Moong Dal Soup","intro":"A thin, nourishing soup of yellow moong dal and mixed vegetables flavoured with ginger, pepper and lemon. It is light yet protein-rich, making it an ideal dinner. Partly blending gives a smooth body. Warm and comforting on cold evenings.","kcal":140,"protein":9,"minutes":25,"ingredients":["1/4 cup yellow moong dal","1 cup mixed vegetables (carrot, beans, lauki)","1 tsp grated ginger","1/4 tsp turmeric","1/2 tsp black pepper","1/2 tsp cumin seeds","3 cups water and salt","Juice of 1/2 lemon"],"steps":["Pressure cook dal, vegetables, ginger, turmeric and water for 2 whistles.","Blend half the mixture and mix it back.","Temper cumin in a few drops of ghee and add.","Season with salt and pepper and simmer 3 minutes.","Squeeze lemon and serve."],"benefits":["High protein soup. Light dinner option.","Easy to digest. Warming."]},{"id":"r055","cat":"veg","title":"Lobia Curry","intro":"Black-eyed beans cooked in a tangy tomato-onion gravy with Punjabi spices. Lobia is rich in protein and fibre and cooks faster than rajma. It is earthy, hearty and great value. Serve with jowar roti or brown rice.","kcal":210,"protein":12,"minutes":35,"ingredients":["1/2 cup lobia, soaked 4 hours","1 onion, chopped","2 tomatoes, pureed","1 tsp ginger-garlic paste","1 tsp coriander powder","1/2 tsp garam masala and chilli powder","1 tsp oil","Salt and coriander"],"steps":["Pressure cook lobia with salt for 3 whistles.","Saute onion and ginger-garlic in oil until golden.","Add tomato puree and spices and cook till oil separates.","Add lobia with its water and simmer 10 minutes.","Garnish with coriander."],"benefits":["Plant protein. High fibre.","Low fat. Budget-friendly."]},{"id":"r056","cat":"veg","title":"Sooji Vegetable Idli","intro":"Instant rava idlis studded with grated carrot, peas and coriander. They are steamed, soft and completely oil-free. Colourful vegetables make them attractive to kids. Serve with sambar or chutney.","kcal":140,"protein":5,"minutes":25,"ingredients":["1 cup fine rava, dry-roasted","1/2 cup curd","1/2 cup grated carrot and peas","2 tbsp coriander","1/2 tsp mustard seeds and 6 curry leaves","1/2 tsp eno fruit salt","Salt","Water as needed"],"steps":["Mix rava, curd, vegetables, coriander and salt with water into a thick batter.","Add a mustard-curry leaf tempering made with few drops of oil.","Rest 15 minutes.","Add eno and mix gently.","Pour into greased moulds and steam 12 minutes."],"benefits":["Oil-free breakfast. Vegetables add fibre.","Light and fluffy. Kid-friendly."]},{"id":"r057","cat":"veg","title":"Mint Paneer Tikka","intro":"Paneer cubes coated in a vibrant green marinade of mint, coriander, chillies and hung curd, then grilled until lightly charred. It is fresh, zesty and high in protein. A lovely variation on classic tikka. Serve with onion rings and lemon.","kcal":240,"protein":20,"minutes":30,"ingredients":["200 g low-fat paneer, cubed","1/2 cup hung curd","1/2 cup mint and coriander leaves","2 green chillies","1 inch ginger","1/2 tsp chaat masala","Juice of 1/2 lemon","1 tsp oil and salt"],"steps":["Blend mint, coriander, chillies and ginger to a paste.","Mix the paste with curd, salt, oil, lemon and chaat masala.","Coat paneer and marinate 20 minutes.","Thread on skewers with onion and capsicum.","Grill or air-fry at 200 C for 10 minutes."],"benefits":["High protein. Mint aids digestion.","Low carb starter. Grilled, not fried."]},{"id":"r058","cat":"veg","title":"Vegetable Poha","intro":"Soft flattened rice tossed with onion, peas, carrots and a few roasted peanuts, tempered with mustard seeds and curry leaves. It is light, quick and gives steady morning energy. More vegetables and fewer peanuts keep it weight-loss friendly. Finish with lemon and coriander.","kcal":220,"protein":6,"minutes":15,"ingredients":["1 cup thick poha","1/2 cup peas and diced carrot","1 onion, chopped","1 tbsp roasted peanuts","1/2 tsp mustard seeds and 8 curry leaves","1/4 tsp turmeric","1 tsp oil","Salt, lemon and coriander"],"steps":["Rinse poha in a sieve and let it soften for 5 minutes.","Heat oil, crackle mustard seeds and curry leaves.","Add onion, peas and carrot and cook 3 minutes.","Add poha, turmeric and salt and toss gently.","Cover 2 minutes, add lemon, peanuts and coriander."],"benefits":["Light, quick breakfast. Good source of iron.","Vegetables add fibre. Steady morning energy."]},{"id":"r059","cat":"veg","title":"Spinach Corn Soup","intro":"A smooth green soup of spinach blended with onion and garlic, studded with sweet corn kernels. It is rich in iron, very low in calories and ready in 20 minutes. A splash of milk makes it creamy without cream. Perfect as a starter before dinner.","kcal":110,"protein":4,"minutes":20,"ingredients":["2 cups spinach","1/4 cup sweet corn","1 onion, chopped","3 garlic cloves","1/4 cup low-fat milk","1 tsp oil","2 cups water","Salt and pepper"],"steps":["Saute onion and garlic in oil for 2 minutes.","Add spinach and water and boil 3 minutes.","Cool and blend smooth.","Return to the pan, add corn and milk and simmer 5 minutes.","Season with salt and pepper."],"benefits":["Rich in iron. Very low calorie.","Fibre-rich. Creamy without cream."]},{"id":"r060","cat":"veg","title":"Veg Quinoa Upma","intro":"Quinoa cooked South Indian upma style with mustard seeds, curry leaves and colourful vegetables. It is fluffy, savoury and much higher in protein than rava upma. Quinoa is gluten-free and keeps you full. Serve with coconut-free chutney.","kcal":240,"protein":9,"minutes":20,"ingredients":["1/2 cup quinoa, rinsed well","1/2 cup mixed vegetables","1 small onion, chopped","1/2 tsp mustard seeds and 1 tsp urad dal","8 curry leaves","1 green chilli","1 tsp oil","Salt and 1 cup water"],"steps":["Heat oil, crackle mustard seeds, urad dal and curry leaves.","Add onion and chilli and saute till soft.","Add vegetables and cook 2 minutes.","Add quinoa, salt and water and bring to a boil.","Cover and cook on low 12 minutes till fluffy."],"benefits":["Complete plant protein. Gluten-free.","High fibre. Light breakfast."]},{"id":"r061","cat":"nonveg","title":"Chicken 65 (Air Fried)","intro":"The fiery South Indian favourite made without deep frying. Boneless chicken is marinated in curd, ginger-garlic and red chilli, then air-fried and tossed with curry leaves and green chillies. You get the same crunch and punch with a fraction of the oil. A perfect high-protein starter.","kcal":260,"protein":30,"minutes":35,"ingredients":["300 g boneless chicken, bite-size","3 tbsp hung curd","1 tsp ginger-garlic paste","1 1/2 tsp kashmiri chilli powder","1 tbsp rice flour","10 curry leaves and 2 green chillies","1 tsp oil","Salt and lemon juice"],"steps":["Marinate chicken with curd, ginger-garlic, chilli, rice flour, salt and lemon for 30 minutes.","Air-fry at 200 C for 14–16 minutes, shaking halfway.","Heat oil, crackle curry leaves and slit chillies.","Toss the cooked chicken in this tadka for a minute.","Serve hot with onion rings."],"benefits":["Lean chicken protein keeps you full and protects muscle.","Air frying saves around 250 kcal versus deep frying.","Curry leaves support digestion. Satisfies fried-food cravings guilt-free."]},{"id":"r062","cat":"nonveg","title":"Tandoori Chicken","intro":"Juicy chicken pieces marinated twice — first in lemon and chilli, then in spiced hung curd — and roasted until charred at the edges. It is naturally low in carbs and fat when the skin is removed. Bake, grill or air-fry for smoky flavour. Serve with mint chutney and salad.","kcal":280,"protein":34,"minutes":45,"ingredients":["500 g chicken legs, skinless, slashed","1 tbsp lemon juice","1/2 cup hung curd","1 tbsp ginger-garlic paste","1 1/2 tsp kashmiri chilli","1 tsp tandoori masala","1 tsp mustard oil","Salt and chaat masala"],"steps":["Rub chicken with lemon, chilli and salt and rest 15 minutes.","Mix curd, ginger-garlic, tandoori masala and mustard oil.","Coat chicken well and marinate at least 2 hours.","Roast at 220 C for 30–35 minutes, turning once.","Sprinkle chaat masala and serve with lemon."],"benefits":["Very high protein, very low carb. Skinless chicken cuts saturated fat.","Curd marinade tenderises naturally. Ideal post-workout meal."]},{"id":"r063","cat":"nonveg","title":"Chicken Tikka","intro":"Boneless chicken chunks with onion and capsicum, marinated in tandoori spices and grilled on skewers. It is a restaurant favourite that fits perfectly into a fat-loss plan. Eat it with salad or wrap it in a jowar roti. Great for meal prep.","kcal":240,"protein":32,"minutes":40,"ingredients":["300 g boneless chicken, cubed","1/2 cup hung curd","1 tsp ginger-garlic paste","1 tsp kashmiri chilli","1/2 tsp garam masala and cumin","1 onion and 1 capsicum, cubed","1 tsp mustard oil","Salt and lemon"],"steps":["Whisk curd with spices, oil, salt and lemon.","Add chicken and vegetables and marinate 1 hour.","Thread onto skewers alternating with vegetables.","Grill or air-fry at 200 C for 15 minutes, turning once.","Serve with mint chutney."],"benefits":["High protein snack or meal. Low carb and low fat.","Vegetables add fibre and vitamins. Easy to batch-cook."]},{"id":"r064","cat":"nonveg","title":"Chicken Curry (Home Style Light)","intro":"A comforting, homestyle chicken curry cooked with onions, tomatoes and whole spices using just a teaspoon of oil. Skinless chicken and a slow-cooked masala give deep flavour without heaviness. Eat with a phulka or a small portion of brown rice. Sunday lunch, made light.","kcal":290,"protein":30,"minutes":45,"ingredients":["400 g skinless chicken, curry cut","2 onions, finely chopped","2 tomatoes, pureed","1 tbsp ginger-garlic paste","1 tsp each coriander, chilli and garam masala","2 tbsp curd","1 tsp oil","Salt and coriander"],"steps":["Marinate chicken with curd, turmeric and salt for 20 minutes.","Saute onions in oil on low heat till deep golden.","Add ginger-garlic and tomato puree and cook till oil separates.","Add spices and chicken and cook on high for 5 minutes.","Add 1 cup water, simmer covered 20 minutes and garnish."],"benefits":["High protein main course. Minimal oil keeps fats low.","Spices like turmeric are anti- inflammatory.","Satisfying family meal."]},{"id":"r065","cat":"nonveg","title":"Butter Chicken Without Butter","intro":"A ll the creamy, mildly sweet taste of butter chicken with none of the butter and cream. Grilled tikka is simmered in a velvety tomato gravy thickened with curd and a few cashews or melon seeds. It tastes indulgent yet fits your calorie target. Serve with a multigrain roti.","kcal":300,"protein":32,"minutes":45,"ingredients":["300 g grilled chicken tikka","4 tomatoes, chopped","1 onion, chopped","1 tsp ginger-garlic paste","1 tbsp melon seeds or 5 cashews","3 tbsp hung curd","1 tsp kasuri methi","1 tsp oil and salt"],"steps":["Cook tomatoes, onion, ginger-garlic and melon seeds with a little water till soft.","Blend to a smooth puree and strain.","Simmer the puree with chilli, salt and kasuri methi for 8 minutes.","Lower the flame and stir in whisked hung curd.","Add grilled chicken, simmer 5 minutes and serve."],"benefits":["Saves over 200 kcal compared with restaurant style.","High protein.","Tomatoes give lycopene. Curd adds creaminess and probiotics."]},{"id":"r066","cat":"nonveg","title":"Grilled Fish Tikka","intro":"Firm fish fillets in a tangy ajwain-spiced marinade, grilled until flaky. Fish is one of the leanest proteins available and rich in omega-3 fats. Ajwain aids digestion and gives a lovely aroma. Serve with salad and green chutney.","kcal":210,"protein":28,"minutes":30,"ingredients":["300 g firm fish (basa, surmai or rawas)","1/2 cup hung curd","1 tsp ginger-garlic paste","1/2 tsp ajwain","1 tsp kashmiri chilli","1/4 tsp turmeric","1 tsp mustard oil","Salt and lemon"],"steps":["Pat fish dry and cut into large cubes.","Rub with lemon, salt and turmeric for 10 minutes.","Mix curd, ginger-garlic, ajwain, chilli and oil and coat the fish.","Grill or air-fry at 200 C for 10–12 minutes.","Serve with lemon wedges."],"benefits":["Lean protein with omega-3 fats. Supports heart health.","Very low carb. Quick to cook."]},{"id":"r067","cat":"nonveg","title":"Fish Curry (Coastal Light)","intro":"A tangy coastal fish curry made with tomatoes, tamarind and a little coconut milk. Using light coconut milk keeps the flavour while cutting fat. Pairs well with a small portion of red rice. Fragrant with curry leaves and mustard seeds.","kcal":230,"protein":26,"minutes":35,"ingredients":["400 g fish pieces","1 onion, sliced","2 tomatoes, chopped","1 tbsp tamarind pulp","1/4 cup light coconut milk","1 tsp each chilli and coriander powder","1/2 tsp mustard seeds and curry leaves","1 tsp oil and salt"],"steps":["Marinate fish with turmeric and salt.","Temper mustard and curry leaves, add onion and cook soft.","Add tomatoes and spices, cook to a paste.","Add tamarind and 1 cup water, bring to a boil.","Add fish and coconut milk and simmer 8 minutes."],"benefits":["Omega-3 fats support fat metabolism. Lean protein.","Light coconut milk keeps fat in check. Tamarind aids digestion."]},{"id":"r068","cat":"nonveg","title":"Chicken Keema Matar","intro":"Lean minced chicken cooked with green peas in a spicy onion-tomato masala. Keema cooks quickly and is very versatile. Eat it with a roti or stuff it in lettuce cups. High protein, low fat.","kcal":270,"protein":30,"minutes":30,"ingredients":["300 g chicken mince","1/2 cup green peas","1 onion, chopped","1 tomato, chopped","1 tsp ginger-garlic paste","1 tsp each coriander and garam masala","1 tsp oil","Salt and coriander"],"steps":["Saute onion and ginger-garlic till golden.","Add tomato and spices and cook soft.","Add keema and break up lumps, cook on high 5 minutes.","Add peas and 1/2 cup water and cook covered 10 minutes.","Dry off the moisture and garnish."],"benefits":["Lean mince is high in protein. Peas add fibre.","Low carb when eaten with salad. Great for meal prep."]},{"id":"r069","cat":"nonveg","title":"Lemon Pepper Chicken","intro":"Tender chicken strips pan-seared with crushed black pepper, garlic and fresh lemon. It is simple, quick and full of flavour. Pepper's piperine supports metabolism. Serve with sauteed vegetables.","kcal":230,"protein":32,"minutes":25,"ingredients":["300 g chicken breast, sliced","1 tsp crushed black pepper","4 garlic cloves, minced","Juice of 1 lemon","1/2 tsp lemon zest","1 tsp olive oil","Salt","Parsley or coriander"],"steps":["Marinate chicken with pepper, garlic, lemon zest and salt for 15 minutes.","Heat oil in a pan until hot.","Sear chicken 3–4 minutes per side till golden.","Squeeze lemon juice over and toss.","Garnish and serve with vegetables."],"benefits":["Very lean protein. Black pepper boosts nutrient","absorption.","Vitamin C from lemon. Ready in 25 minutes."]},{"id":"r070","cat":"nonveg","title":"Chicken Soup with Vegetables","intro":"A clear, healing chicken broth with shredded chicken, carrots, beans and ginger. It is light yet satisfying and perfect when you want a low-calorie dinner. The warm broth helps curb overeating. Season with lots of black pepper.","kcal":160,"protein":22,"minutes":35,"ingredients":["200 g chicken with bone","1 carrot and 6 beans, chopped","1 inch ginger, sliced","4 garlic cloves","1 small onion","4 cups water","Black pepper and salt","Spring onion"],"steps":["Boil chicken with ginger, garlic, onion and water for 25 minutes.","Remove chicken, shred the meat and discard bones.","Add vegetables to the broth and cook 5 minutes.","Return chicken, season with salt and pepper.","Garnish with spring onion."],"benefits":["Low calorie, high protein dinner. Hydrating and warming.","Ginger helps digestion. Keeps you full."]},{"id":"r071","cat":"nonveg","title":"Chicken Salad Bowl","intro":"Grilled chicken strips tossed with lettuce, cucumber, onion, capsicum and a mint-curd dressing. A refreshing complete meal for lunch. High protein and full of vegetables. Very easy to pack.","kcal":260,"protein":30,"minutes":20,"ingredients":["150 g grilled chicken breast, sliced","1 cup lettuce","1 cucumber, sliced","1/2 capsicum and 1 small onion","2 tbsp hung curd","1 tbsp mint, chopped","Lemon juice and chaat masala","Salt and pepper"],"steps":["Season chicken with salt and pepper, grill till cooked and slice.","Chop vegetables into bite-size pieces.","Whisk curd, mint, lemon, salt and chaat masala.","Toss vegetables with dressing.","Top with chicken and serve."],"benefits":["Complete meal with protein and fibre. Low carb.","Curd dressing replaces mayo. Light yet satisfying."]},{"id":"r072","cat":"nonveg","title":"Chicken Shami Kebab (Pan Roasted)","intro":"Melt-in-the-mouth kebabs made from chicken mince and chana dal, shallow-roasted with a brush of oil. Chana dal adds fibre and binds the kebabs. Serve with onion rings and mint chutney. Freezes well.","kcal":220,"protein":26,"minutes":45,"ingredients":["300 g chicken mince","1/4 cup chana dal, soaked","1 onion","1 inch ginger and 4 garlic cloves","1 tsp garam masala","2 green chillies","Mint and coriander","1 tsp oil and salt"],"steps":["Pressure cook mince, dal, onion, ginger, garlic and spices with a little water.","Dry off the moisture completely.","Grind to a smooth mixture and add herbs and chillies.","Shape into flat kebabs.","Pan-roast with a brush of oil till golden."],"benefits":["High protein snack. Pan roasted not fried.","Dal adds fibre. Great for meal prep."]},{"id":"r073","cat":"nonveg","title":"Prawn Masala","intro":"Juicy prawns cooked quickly in a spicy onion-tomato masala. Prawns are very lean and cook in minutes. Pair with salad or a small portion of rice. Coastal flavours with very little oil.","kcal":210,"protein":26,"minutes":25,"ingredients":["300 g prawns, cleaned","1 onion, chopped","2 tomatoes, chopped","1 tsp ginger-garlic paste","1 tsp chilli powder","1/2 tsp turmeric","1 tsp oil","Salt and coriander"],"steps":["Marinate prawns with turmeric and salt.","Saute onion and ginger-garlic in oil.","Add tomato and spices and cook to a thick masala.","Add prawns and cook 5–6 minutes until pink.","Garnish and serve."],"benefits":["Very low fat, high protein seafood. Rich in iodine and selenium.","Quick cooking. Low calorie."]},{"id":"r074","cat":"nonveg","title":"Chicken Stir Fry with Vegetables","intro":"Chicken strips with colourful bell peppers, broccoli and onion tossed in garlic and soy. A quick Indo-Chinese meal without sauces full of sugar. Serve as is or with cauliflower rice. Ready in 20 minutes.","kcal":250,"protein":30,"minutes":20,"ingredients":["250 g chicken breast, sliced","1 cup mixed peppers and broccoli","1 onion, sliced","5 garlic cloves","1 tsp soy sauce","1 tsp vinegar","1 tsp oil","Pepper and salt"],"steps":["Season chicken with salt and pepper.","Stir-fry chicken in hot oil till cooked, remove.","Stir-fry garlic, onion and vegetables 3 minutes.","Return chicken, add soy and vinegar.","Toss on high heat and serve."],"benefits":["Lean protein with lots of vegetables. Low sugar.","Quick weeknight meal. Fibre-rich."]},{"id":"r075","cat":"nonveg","title":"Mutton Soup (Paya Style Light)","intro":"A warming, aromatic mutton bone soup with ginger, pepper and whole spices. Slow-cooked bones give collagen-rich broth. Skim the fat for a light version. Ideal on cold evenings.","kcal":200,"protein":20,"minutes":60,"ingredients":["300 g mutton bones with some meat","1 onion","1 inch ginger and 6 garlic cloves","1 tsp black pepper","2 cloves and 1 cinnamon stick","1/4 tsp turmeric","5 cups water","Salt and coriander"],"steps":["Pressure cook all ingredients for 8-10 whistles.","Cool and skim off fat from the top.","Strain the broth and shred the meat.","Reheat with salt and extra pepper.","Garnish with coriander."],"benefits":["Collagen supports joints.","Protein-rich.","Very filling broth.","Skimming removes extra fat."]},{"id":"r076","cat":"nonveg","title":"Egg-Free Chicken Seekh Kebab","intro":"Spiced chicken mince pressed around skewers and grilled until smoky and juicy. Unlike restaurant versions, these need no egg, breadcrumbs or butter, so they stay lean. Grated onion and fresh herbs keep them moist. Serve with onion salad, lemon and mint chutney.","kcal":240,"protein":28,"minutes":35,"ingredients":["300 g chicken mince","1 onion, grated and squeezed dry","1 tsp ginger-garlic paste","2 green chillies, finely chopped","1 tsp garam masala and 1/2 tsp cumin powder","2 tbsp mint and coriander, chopped","1 tsp oil","Salt"],"steps":["Mix mince with onion, ginger-garlic, chillies, spices, herbs and salt.","Knead well and chill for 20 minutes so it firms up.","Wet your hands and press the mixture around skewers into long kebabs.","Brush lightly with oil.","Grill or air-fry at 200 C for 12-15 minutes, turning once."],"benefits":["High protein, low carb.","Grilled, not fried.","No breadcrumbs or egg binder.","Great for parties."]},{"id":"r077","cat":"nonveg","title":"Chicken Lettuce Wraps","intro":"Spicy, dry-cooked chicken mince spooned into crisp lettuce cups instead of rotis. They are fresh, crunchy and very low in carbohydrates. Top with chopped onion, coriander and a squeeze of lemon. A fun, light dinner the whole family enjoys.","kcal":220,"protein":28,"minutes":20,"ingredients":["250 g chicken mince","1 onion, finely chopped","1 tsp ginger-garlic paste","1/2 tsp each cumin, coriander and chilli powder","1/2 capsicum, finely chopped","8 crisp lettuce leaves","1 tsp oil","Salt, lemon and coriander"],"steps":["Saute onion and ginger-garlic in oil until soft.","Add mince and spices and cook on high heat, breaking up lumps.","Add capsicum and salt and cook until dry, about 8 minutes.","Wash and pat dry the lettuce leaves.","Spoon mince into each leaf, squeeze lemon and garnish."],"benefits":["Very low carb.","Fresh crunch from lettuce.","High protein.","Light, fun dinner."]},{"id":"r078","cat":"nonveg","title":"Methi Chicken","intro":"Chicken simmered in a light onion-tomato gravy with plenty of fresh fenugreek leaves. Methi gives a gently bitter, aromatic flavour that pairs beautifully with chicken. It adds fibre and helps control cravings. Serve with phulka for a satisfying dinner.","kcal":270,"protein":30,"minutes":40,"ingredients":["400 g skinless chicken","2 cups fresh methi leaves, chopped","2 onions, chopped","2 tomatoes, chopped","1 tbsp ginger-garlic paste","1 tsp coriander powder and 1/2 tsp garam masala","1 tsp oil","Salt"],"steps":["Saute onions in oil until golden, then add ginger-garlic.","Add tomatoes and spices and cook till soft.","Add chicken and cook on high for 8-10 minutes.","Add methi and 1/2 cup water and cook covered 10 minutes.","Simmer until chicken is tender and serve."],"benefits":["Methi helps control cravings.","Fibre-rich greens.","High protein.","Low oil curry."]},{"id":"r079","cat":"nonveg","title":"Chicken Kathi Roll (Whole Wheat)","intro":"Smoky chicken tikka wrapped in a whole wheat roti with crunchy onions, mint chutney and lemon. It is the healthy version of the famous Kolkata street food. Hung curd replaces mayonnaise, keeping it light. Perfect for lunch on the go.","kcal":320,"protein":28,"minutes":30,"ingredients":["150 g chicken tikka","2 whole wheat rotis","1 onion, thinly sliced","2 tbsp mint chutney","1 tbsp hung curd","1/2 tsp chaat masala","Juice of 1/2 lemon","Lettuce leaves"],"steps":["Warm rotis on a tawa without oil.","Mix chutney and hung curd and spread on each roti.","Lay lettuce, chicken tikka and onion along the centre.","Sprinkle chaat masala and lemon juice.","Roll tightly, wrap in foil and serve."],"benefits":["Balanced protein and carbs.","No mayonnaise.","No refined flour.","Portable meal."]},{"id":"r080","cat":"nonveg","title":"Chicken Saag","intro":"Tender chicken cooked in a smooth, spiced spinach gravy, a lighter non-veg cousin of palak paneer. It packs protein and iron into one bowl. The spinach gives a creamy texture without cream. Serve with roti or millet.","kcal":280,"protein":32,"minutes":40,"ingredients":["400 g skinless chicken","2 bunches spinach, blanched","1 onion, chopped","2 tomatoes, chopped","1 tbsp ginger-garlic paste","1 tsp garam masala","1 tsp oil","Salt"],"steps":["Blend blanched spinach to a smooth puree.","Saute onion and ginger-garlic in oil, add tomatoes and cook soft.","Add chicken and garam masala and cook 10 minutes.","Pour in the spinach puree and salt.","Simmer covered 10 minutes till chicken is tender."],"benefits":["Protein and iron together.","Fibre-rich.","Low carb.","Creamy without cream."]},{"id":"r081","cat":"nonveg","title":"Grilled Fish with Herbs","intro":"Fish fillets rubbed with garlic, lemon zest, mixed herbs and black pepper, then grilled until just flaky. It is simple, elegant and ready in 25 minutes. Fish provides lean protein and heart-healthy omega-3 fats. Serve with sauteed or steamed vegetables.","kcal":200,"protein":28,"minutes":25,"ingredients":["2 fish fillets (basa or salmon)","3 garlic cloves, minced","Zest and juice of 1 lemon","1 tsp mixed dried herbs","1/2 tsp black pepper","1 tsp olive oil","Salt","Steamed vegetables to serve"],"steps":["Pat fillets dry.","Rub with garlic, lemon zest, herbs, pepper, salt and oil.","Rest for 10 minutes.","Grill or pan-sear 3-4 minutes per side.","Squeeze lemon juice and serve with vegetables."],"benefits":["Lean protein.","Low carb.","Omega-3 for heart health.","Quick and elegant."]}]"""

private const val PART_3 = """[{"id":"r082","cat":"nonveg","title":"Chicken Biryani (Brown Rice)","intro":"A fragrant dum biryani made with brown rice, generous chicken and just a teaspoon of ghee. We use more chicken and less rice than usual, so every plate is protein-heavy. Mint, saffron and whole spices give the classic aroma. Serve with cucumber raita.","kcal":380,"protein":30,"minutes":60,"ingredients":["300 g skinless chicken","1 cup brown basmati rice, soaked 1 hour","1 onion, thinly sliced","1/2 cup curd","1 1/2 tsp biryani masala","Bay leaf, cloves, cardamom and cinnamon","Handful mint and few saffron strands","1 tsp ghee and salt"],"steps":["Marinate chicken with curd, biryani masala and salt for 30 minutes.","Boil rice with whole spices and salt until 70% cooked, drain.","Brown onions in ghee, add chicken and cook till almost done.","Layer rice over chicken with mint and saffron milk.","Cover tightly and cook on low heat 20 minutes."],"benefits":["High protein biryani.","Very little ghee.","Brown rice adds fibre.","A portion-controlled treat."]},{"id":"r083","cat":"nonveg","title":"Chilli Chicken (Healthy)","intro":"The Indo-Chinese favourite made without deep frying or a thick cornflour batter. Chicken is pan-seared and tossed with onion, capsicum, garlic and green chillies in a light sauce. It is spicy, glossy and satisfying. Serve with cauliflower rice.","kcal":260,"protein":30,"minutes":30,"ingredients":["250 g boneless chicken, cubed","1 capsicum and 1 onion, cubed","6 garlic cloves and 2 green chillies","1 tsp light soy sauce","1 tsp vinegar","1 tsp red chilli sauce","1 tsp cornflour in 1/4 cup water","1 tsp oil"],"steps":["Season chicken with salt and pepper and sear in oil till golden, remove.","Stir-fry garlic and chillies, then onion and capsicum on high heat.","Add soy, vinegar and chilli sauce.","Add cornflour slurry and stir till glossy.","Toss in the chicken and serve hot."],"benefits":["No deep frying.","Low carb.","High protein.","A healthy takeaway swap."]},{"id":"r084","cat":"nonveg","title":"Mutton Keema with Lauki","intro":"Lean mutton mince cooked with diced bottle gourd in a spicy masala. The lauki soaks up flavour and adds volume, so you eat a satisfying portion with fewer calories. Mutton provides iron and vitamin B12. Serve with phulka.","kcal":290,"protein":26,"minutes":40,"ingredients":["250 g lean mutton mince","1 cup lauki, diced","1 onion, chopped","1 tomato, chopped","1 tbsp ginger-garlic paste","1 tsp coriander powder and 1/2 tsp garam masala","1 tsp oil","Salt and coriander"],"steps":["Saute onion and ginger-garlic in oil till golden.","Add tomato and spices and cook soft.","Add keema and cook on high 10 minutes, breaking lumps.","Add lauki and 1/2 cup water and cook covered 10 minutes.","Dry off any moisture and garnish."],"benefits":["Rich in iron and B12.","High protein.","Lauki adds volume with few calories.","Filling dinner."]},{"id":"r085","cat":"nonveg","title":"Chicken Malai Tikka (Light)","intro":"Creamy, mild white tikka where cream is replaced by hung curd and a spoon of cheese spread. Cardamom and white pepper give it a delicate flavour. It is juicy, tender and loved by kids. Grill or air-fry and serve with mint chutney.","kcal":250,"protein":32,"minutes":40,"ingredients":["300 g boneless chicken","1/2 cup hung curd","1 tbsp light cheese spread","1 tsp ginger-garlic paste","1/4 tsp cardamom powder","1/2 tsp white pepper","1 green chilli paste","1 tsp oil and salt"],"steps":["Rub chicken with ginger-garlic, salt and lemon for 15 minutes.","Whisk curd, cheese spread, cardamom, pepper, chilli and oil.","Coat chicken and marinate 1 hour.","Thread on skewers.","Grill or air-fry at 200 C for 15 minutes."],"benefits":["High protein.","Mild and kid-friendly.","No cream.","Low carb."]},{"id":"r086","cat":"nonveg","title":"Fish Moilee (Light)","intro":"A gentle Kerala fish stew in a fragrant turmeric and light coconut milk broth with ginger, green chillies and curry leaves. It is mild, soothing and full of lean protein. in check. Serve with a small portion of red rice.","kcal":230,"protein":25,"minutes":30,"ingredients":["400 g firm fish pieces","1/2 cup light coconut milk","1 onion, sliced","2 green chillies, slit","1 inch ginger, julienned","10 curry leaves","1/4 tsp turmeric","1 tsp coconut oil and salt"],"steps":["Rub fish with turmeric and salt.","Heat oil and saute onion, ginger, chillies and curry leaves till soft.","Add turmeric and 1 cup water and bring to a simmer.","Slide in the fish and cook 6 minutes.","Add coconut milk and simmer 2 minutes without boiling."],"benefits":["Omega-3 rich fish.","Lean protein.","Light coconut milk.","Soothing and mild."]},{"id":"r087","cat":"nonveg","title":"Pepper Chicken Dry","intro":"A Chettinad-style dry chicken roast with freshly crushed black pepper, curry leaves and onions. It is bold, fiery and very low in carbs. Pepper's piperine supports digestion and metabolism. Serve with salad or a millet roti.","kcal":260,"protein":32,"minutes":30,"ingredients":["300 g boneless chicken","2 tsp freshly crushed black pepper","1 onion, sliced","1 tbsp ginger-garlic paste","15 curry leaves","1/4 tsp turmeric","1 tsp fennel seeds","1 tsp oil and salt"],"steps":["Heat oil, add fennel and curry leaves, then onion.","Add ginger-garlic and cook 1 minute.","Add chicken, turmeric and salt and cook covered 10 minutes.","Add crushed pepper and roast on high until dry.","Garnish with more curry leaves."],"benefits":["Pepper supports metabolism.","Very low carb.","Lean protein.","Bold flavour."]},{"id":"r088","cat":"nonveg","title":"Chicken Tikka Masala (Light)","intro":"Grilled chicken tikka simmered in a smoky, spiced onion-tomato masala finished with curd and kasuri methi. You get restaurant flavour at home-cooked calories. No butter, no cream. Serve with phulka and salad.","kcal":300,"protein":32,"minutes":50,"ingredients":["300 g grilled chicken tikka","2 onions, finely chopped","3 tomatoes, pureed","1 tbsp ginger-garlic paste","1 tsp kashmiri chilli and 1 tsp garam masala","1 tsp kasuri methi","2 tbsp curd, whisked","1 tsp oil and salt"],"steps":["Saute onions in oil until golden, add ginger-garlic.","Add tomato puree and spices and cook till oil separates.","Lower heat and stir in whisked curd.","Add tikka and 1/2 cup water and simmer 5 minutes.","Crush kasuri methi over the top and serve."],"benefits":["High protein.","Low oil.","No butter or cream.","Satisfying main course."]},{"id":"r089","cat":"nonveg","title":"Prawn Stir Fry","intro":"Juicy prawns tossed with garlic, chilli flakes, onion and capsicum on high heat. Prawns cook in just 3-4 minutes, so dinner is ready in 15. They are very lean and rich in minerals like selenium and iodine. Serve with salad or cauliflower rice.","kcal":190,"protein":24,"minutes":15,"ingredients":["250 g prawns, cleaned","1 capsicum, sliced","1 onion, sliced","5 garlic cloves, chopped","1/2 tsp chilli flakes","1 tsp light soy sauce","1 tsp oil","Salt and spring onion"],"steps":["Season prawns with salt and chilli flakes.","Heat oil on high and saute garlic for 30 seconds.","Add prawns and cook 2 minutes until pink.","Add onion and capsicum and toss 2 minutes.","Add soy sauce, toss and garnish with spring onion."],"benefits":["Very lean protein.","Low fat.","Ready in 15 minutes.","Rich in minerals."]},{"id":"r090","cat":"nonveg","title":"Chicken Ghee Roast (Light)","intro":"A fiery Mangalorean roast where chicken is coated in a paste of roasted byadgi chillies, spices, tamarind and garlic. We use only one spoon of ghee instead of the usual several. It is tangy, spicy and deeply flavourful. Serve with salad or neer dosa.","kcal":280,"protein":30,"minutes":40,"ingredients":["300 g boneless chicken","6 byadgi chillies","1 tsp coriander seeds and 1/2 tsp cumin seeds","1 tsp tamarind pulp","6 garlic cloves","3 tbsp curd","1 tsp ghee","Salt and curry leaves"],"steps":["Dry-roast chillies, coriander and cumin, grind with tamarind and garlic.","Marinate chicken with curd, salt and half the paste for 30 minutes.","Heat ghee, fry remaining paste for 2 minutes.","Add chicken and cook covered 10 minutes.","Uncover and roast until dry, adding curry leaves."],"benefits":["High protein.","Big flavour.","Minimal ghee.","Low carb."]},{"id":"r091","cat":"egg","title":"High Protein Paneer Omelette","intro":"A fluffy masala omelette stuffed with crumbled paneer, onion, tomato and green chillies. Combining eggs and paneer creates a breakfast with over 25 hours and reduces mid-morning snacking. Cook it in a non-stick pan with just a few drops of oil.","kcal":280,"protein":26,"minutes":15,"ingredients":["2 whole eggs and 1 egg white","40 g paneer, crumbled","1 small onion, finely chopped","1 small tomato, finely chopped","1 green chilli and coriander","1/4 tsp turmeric and pepper","1/2 tsp oil","Salt"],"steps":["Whisk eggs and egg white with turmeric, pepper and salt until frothy.","Stir in onion, tomato, chilli and coriander.","Heat oil in a non-stick pan and pour in the mixture.","Sprinkle paneer over one half while the top is still soft.","Fold, cook 1 minute on each side and serve."],"benefits":["Over 25 g protein in one meal.","Keeps you full till lunch.","Very low carb.","Eggs provide choline and vitamin B12."]},{"id":"r092","cat":"egg","title":"Egg Bhurji","intro":"Spicy Indian scrambled eggs cooked with onions, tomatoes and green chillies. It is a quick, satisfying breakfast or dinner. Add extra egg whites to boost protein without adding fat. Wrap in lettuce or eat with a single multigrain toast.","kcal":220,"protein":15,"minutes":15,"ingredients":["3 eggs (or 2 eggs + 2 whites)","1 onion, finely chopped","1 tomato, finely chopped","1 green chilli","1/4 tsp turmeric","1/2 tsp pav bhaji masala","1/2 tsp oil","Salt and coriander"],"steps":["Heat oil and saute onion till soft.","Add chilli, tomato, turmeric and masala, cook 2 minutes.","Pour in beaten eggs and salt.","Stir gently on low heat till softly set.","Garnish with coriander and serve."],"benefits":["High quality protein.","Ready in 15 minutes.","Very low carb.","Spices boost flavour without calories."]},{"id":"r093","cat":"egg","title":"Egg Curry (Light)","intro":"Boiled eggs simmered in a homestyle onion-tomato gravy made with just a teaspoon of oil. It is comforting, protein-rich and budget-friendly. Use 1 whole egg and extra whites to manage calories. Serve with phulka or cauliflower rice.","kcal":240,"protein":14,"minutes":30,"ingredients":["3 boiled eggs, halved","2 onions, chopped","2 tomatoes, pureed","1 tsp ginger-garlic paste","1 tsp coriander powder and 1/2 tsp garam masala","1/2 tsp chilli powder and turmeric","1 tsp oil","Salt and coriander"],"steps":["Lightly prick the boiled eggs and toss in a pinch of turmeric and chilli.","Saute onions and ginger-garlic in oil until golden.","Add tomato puree and spices, cook till oil separates.","Add 1 cup water and simmer 5 minutes.","Add eggs, simmer 3 minutes and garnish."],"benefits":["Affordable complete protein.","Satisfying main course.","Low oil gravy.","Rich in vitamins D and B12."]},{"id":"r094","cat":"egg","title":"Egg White Veggie Omelette","intro":"A light, fluffy omelette made from spinach, capsicum and onion. It is almost pure protein with very few calories. A great choice for dinner or a pre-workout meal. Season with pepper and herbs.","kcal":130,"protein":15,"minutes":10,"ingredients":["4 egg whites","1/4 cup spinach, chopped","1/4 capsicum, chopped","1 small onion, chopped","1 green chilli","Pepper and oregano","Few drops oil","Salt"],"steps":["Whisk egg whites with salt and pepper till frothy.","Saute vegetables in a few drops of oil for 2 minutes.","Pour egg whites over the vegetables.","Cover and cook on low heat until set.","Fold, sprinkle oregano and serve."],"benefits":["Lean protein with almost no fat.","Vegetables add fibre and iron.","Very low calorie.","Ideal light dinner."]},{"id":"r095","cat":"egg","title":"Masala Boiled Egg Salad","intro":"Boiled eggs tossed with cucumber, onion, tomato and a chaat masala-lemon dressing. It is a crunchy, tangy salad that works as a meal or snack. Takes 15 minutes and travels well. Add sprouts for more fibre.","kcal":200,"protein":14,"minutes":15,"ingredients":["3 boiled eggs, quartered","1 cucumber, chopped","1 tomato, chopped","1 small onion, chopped","1 tsp chaat masala","Juice of 1/2 lemon","Coriander","Salt and pepper"],"steps":["Boil eggs for 10 minutes, cool and quarter.","Chop all vegetables.","Combine vegetables with salt, pepper, chaat masala and lemon.","Gently fold in eggs.","Garnish with coriander and serve."],"benefits":["High protein snack.","Fresh vegetables add fibre.","Low carb.","Portable lunch option."]},{"id":"r096","cat":"egg","title":"Egg Muffins with Vegetables","intro":"Mini egg muffins baked with spinach, tomato, onion and a little cheese. Make a batch on Sunday and reheat for quick breakfasts all week. They are portion-controlled and kid-friendly. No flour needed.","kcal":180,"protein":14,"minutes":25,"ingredients":["4 eggs","1/2 cup spinach, chopped","1 small tomato, chopped","1 small onion, chopped","2 tbsp grated cheese","Pepper and chilli flakes","Salt","Oil to grease"],"steps":["Preheat oven to 180 C and grease a muffin tray.","Whisk eggs with salt, pepper and chilli flakes.","Divide vegetables into the muffin cups.","Pour egg mixture over and top with cheese.","Bake 18-20 minutes until puffed and set."],"benefits":["Portion controlled.","High protein breakfast.","Meal-prep friendly.","No flour, low carb."]},{"id":"r097","cat":"egg","title":"Egg Dosa","intro":"A crisp dosa topped with a beaten egg, onions and chillies. It adds protein to a regular dosa and keeps you full for longer. Use ragi or oats dosa batter for extra fibre. Serve with chutney.","kcal":230,"protein":11,"minutes":15,"ingredients":["1 ladle dosa batter (ragi or regular)","1 egg","1 small onion, chopped","1 green chilli","Pepper","Coriander","Few drops oil","Salt"],"steps":["Spread batter thinly on a hot tawa.","Break the egg on top and spread it evenly.","Sprinkle onion, chilli, pepper, salt and coriander.","Drizzle few drops of oil and cook till crisp.","Fold and serve."],"benefits":["Adds protein to a carb meal.","Quick breakfast.","Keeps you full longer.","Can use millet batter."]},{"id":"r098","cat":"egg","title":"Egg Bhurji Wrap","intro":"Spicy egg bhurji rolled in a whole wheat roti with onions and mint chutney. Perfect for lunch boxes and busy mornings. It is balanced with protein, carbs and fibre. Add lettuce for crunch.","kcal":290,"protein":18,"minutes":20,"ingredients":["2 eggs","1 whole wheat roti","1 onion","1 tomato","1 tbsp mint chutney","Lettuce","Spices","Salt and 1/2 tsp oil"],"steps":["Make egg bhurji with onion, tomato and spices.","Warm the roti on a tawa.","Spread chutney and lay lettuce.","Add bhurji and roll tightly.","Cut in half and serve."],"benefits":["Balanced meal.","Portable.","Whole wheat fibre.","High protein."]},{"id":"r099","cat":"egg","title":"Egg Drop Soup (Indian Style)","intro":"A light ginger-garlic broth with ribbons of beaten egg and vegetables. It is very low in calories yet warm and filling. Great for dinner on light days. Ready in 15 minutes.","kcal":120,"protein":10,"minutes":15,"ingredients":["2 eggs, beaten","3 cups vegetable stock or water","1 tsp ginger, grated","3 garlic cloves","1/2 cup cabbage and carrot","Pepper and salt","1 tsp soy sauce","Spring onion"],"steps":["Boil stock with ginger, garlic and vegetables for 5 minutes.","Season with soy, salt and pepper.","Stir the soup in a circle and slowly pour in beaten eggs.","Let ribbons form for 30 seconds.","Garnish with spring onion."],"benefits":["Very low calorie.","Hydrating.","Protein in a light meal.","Comforting."]},{"id":"r100","cat":"egg","title":"Palak Egg Curry","intro":"Halved boiled eggs nestled in a smooth, spiced spinach gravy. This dish combines the complete protein of eggs with the iron and fibre of spinach. It is creamy without any cream and ready in 30 minutes. Serve with phulka or millet roti.","kcal":230,"protein":15,"minutes":30,"ingredients":["3 boiled eggs, halved","2 bunches spinach, blanched","1 onion, chopped","1 tomato, chopped","1 tsp ginger-garlic paste","1/2 tsp garam masala and cumin powder","1 tsp oil","Salt"],"steps":["Blend the blanched spinach into a smooth puree.","Saute onion and ginger-garlic in oil, add tomato and cook soft.","Add spices and spinach puree and simmer 5 minutes.","Gently place the halved eggs in the gravy.","Simmer 2 minutes and serve."],"benefits":["Protein plus iron.","Fibre-rich greens.","Low carb.","No cream needed."]},{"id":"r101","cat":"drink","title":"Green Weight Loss Smoothie","intro":"A refreshing blend of spinach, cucumber, green apple, mint and lemon with a spoon of chia seeds. It is light, hydrating and full of fibre. Drink it in the morning or as a mid-meal snack to curb cravings. No sugar added.","kcal":140,"protein":6,"minutes":5,"ingredients":["1 cup spinach","1/2 cucumber","1/2 green apple","8 mint leaves","1 tsp chia seeds, soaked","Juice of 1/2 lemon","1 cup water or coconut water","Ice cubes"],"steps":["Wash and chop spinach, cucumber and apple.","Add everything to a blender with water.","Blend until smooth.","Stir in soaked chia seeds.","Serve chilled."],"benefits":["Fibre keeps you full.","No added sugar.","Hydrating and detoxifying.","Rich in vitamins and minerals."]},{"id":"r102","cat":"drink","title":"Jeera Water","intro":"An age-old Indian remedy made by boiling cumin seeds in water. Drink it warm on an empty stomach to kick-start digestion. It reduces bloating and supports metabolism. Add lemon for flavour.","kcal":10,"protein":0,"minutes":10,"ingredients":["1 tsp cumin seeds","2 cups water","Juice of 1/2 lemon (optional)","Pinch of black salt (optional)"],"steps":["Soak cumin seeds in water overnight.","Boil the water with seeds for 5 minutes.","Strain into a cup.","Add lemon and black salt if desired.","Sip warm on an empty stomach."],"benefits":["Improves digestion.","Nearly zero calories.","Reduces bloating.","Supports metabolism."]},{"id":"r103","cat":"drink","title":"Cinnamon Ajwain Tea","intro":"A warming, caffeine-free herbal tea brewed from cinnamon bark and ajwain seeds. Sip it after meals to soothe digestion and reduce bloating. Cinnamon is known to help steady blood sugar, which can curb sugar cravings. A comforting evening ritual that replaces milky sweet tea.","kcal":5,"protein":0,"minutes":10,"ingredients":["1 small cinnamon stick","1/2 tsp ajwain (carom) seeds","2 cups water","1 tsp honey (optional)","Few drops lemon juice","2 mint leaves (optional)"],"steps":["Bring water to a boil with the cinnamon stick and ajwain.","Simmer on low heat for 5-7 minutes until golden.","Strain into cups.","Let it cool slightly before adding honey and lemon.","Sip warm after meals."],"benefits":["Cinnamon helps regulate blood","sugar.","Caffeine-free and calming.","Ajwain relieves gas and bloating.","Nearly zero calories."]},{"id":"r104","cat":"drink","title":"Masala Chaas (Buttermilk)","intro":"A chilled, spiced buttermilk blended with roasted cumin, ginger, mint and coriander. It is India's original digestive drink and a perfect replacement for sugary soft drinks. With only about 50 calories per glass, it cools the body and supports gut health. Drink it with or after lunch.","kcal":50,"protein":3,"minutes":5,"ingredients":["1/2 cup low-fat curd","1 1/2 cups chilled water","1/2 tsp roasted cumin powder","Pinch of black salt","1/2 inch ginger, grated","1 green chilli (optional)","2 tbsp mint and coriander","Salt to taste"],"steps":["Add curd, water, ginger and chilli to a blender.","Blend until frothy and smooth.","Stir in cumin, black salt and salt.","Add finely chopped mint and coriander.","Serve chilled with a pinch of cumin on top."],"benefits":["Probiotic for gut health.","Very low calorie.","Cooling and hydrating.","Aids digestion."]},{"id":"r105","cat":"drink","title":"Lemon Ginger Detox Water","intro":"A refreshing infused water with lemon slices, fresh ginger and mint. Keeping a bottle nearby makes it easy to drink more water through the day, which helps control hunger. It has no sugar and almost no calories. Refill the jug two or three times with the same ingredients.","kcal":10,"protein":0,"minutes":5,"ingredients":["1 lemon, thinly sliced","1 inch ginger, thinly sliced","10 mint leaves","1 litre water","Few cucumber slices (optional)","Ice cubes"],"steps":["Add lemon, ginger, mint and cucumber to a large jug.","Lightly crush the mint with a spoon.","Pour water over and stir.","Refrigerate for at least 2 hours to infuse.","Sip through the day and refill with fresh water."],"benefits":["Encourages hydration.","Ginger aids digestion.","Provides vitamin C.","Zero sugar, zero calories."]},{"id":"r106","cat":"drink","title":"Banana Oats Protein Smoothie","intro":"A thick, creamy breakfast smoothie made with banana, oats, curd, milk and a spoon of peanut butter. It gives a balance of protein, fibre and healthy fats that keeps you full for hours. The banana sweetens it naturally, so no sugar is needed. Ideal before or after a workout.","kcal":260,"protein":14,"minutes":5,"ingredients":["1 small ripe banana","2 tbsp rolled oats","1/2 cup low-fat curd","1/2 cup low-fat milk","1 tsp peanut butter","Pinch of cinnamon","1 tsp flaxseed powder","Ice cubes"],"steps":["Add oats to the blender first and pulse to a powder.","Add banana, curd, milk, peanut butter and flaxseed.","Blend until smooth and creamy.","Add ice and blend again, thin with water if needed.","Pour into a glass and dust with cinnamon."],"benefits":["Balanced breakfast in a glass.","Natural sweetness, no sugar.","Protein and fibre for fullness.","Good pre-workout energy."]},{"id":"r107","cat":"drink","title":"Beetroot Carrot Juice","intro":"A vibrant ruby juice of beetroot, carrot, amla and ginger. It is packed with antioxidants, iron and vitamin C. Blending without straining keeps the fibre, so it fills you up and does not spike blood sugar. Drink it fresh in the morning.","kcal":90,"protein":2,"minutes":10,"ingredients":["1 small beetroot, peeled","2 carrots, peeled","1 amla, deseeded","1/2 inch ginger","Juice of 1/2 lemon","Pinch of black salt","1 cup water","Ice cubes"],"steps":["Chop beetroot, carrots, amla and ginger.","Blend with water until completely smooth.","Do not strain, to keep all the fibre.","Stir in lemon juice and black salt.","Serve immediately over ice."],"benefits":["Rich in iron and antioxidants.","Fibre retained.","Supports stamina and skin.","Low calorie."]},{"id":"r108","cat":"drink","title":"Methi Seed Water","intro":"Fenugreek seeds soaked overnight make a simple, traditional morning drink. The soaked seeds release soluble fibre into the water, which helps you feel full and supports healthy blood sugar levels. It takes less than a minute to prepare. Chew the softened seeds for extra benefit.","kcal":10,"protein":0,"minutes":5,"ingredients":["1 tsp methi (fenugreek) seeds","1 glass water","Few drops lemon juice (optional)","Pinch of cinnamon (optional)"],"steps":["Rinse methi seeds and place them in a glass of water at night.","Leave to soak for 8 hours.","In the morning, warm the water slightly if you like.","Add lemon or cinnamon if desired and drink on an empty stomach.","Chew the soaked seeds and wait 30 minutes before breakfast."],"benefits":["Helps control blood sugar.","Improves digestion.","Reduces appetite.","Zero calories."]},{"id":"r109","cat":"drink","title":"Coconut Water Mint Cooler","intro":"Fresh tender coconut water shaken with crushed mint, lemon and a pinch of black salt. It is naturally sweet and full of electrolytes like potassium. A perfect post-workout drink and far healthier than packaged sports drinks. Serve ice-cold on summer afternoons.","kcal":60,"protein":1,"minutes":5,"ingredients":["1 glass tender coconut water","8 mint leaves","Juice of 1/2 lemon","Pinch of black salt","Few slices of cucumber","Ice cubes"],"steps":["Gently crush mint leaves in the bottom of a glass.","Add lemon juice and black salt.","Pour in chilled coconut water.","Add cucumber slices and ice.","Stir well and serve immediately."],"benefits":["Natural electrolytes.","Low calorie.","Hydrating after exercise.","No added sugar."]},{"id":"r110","cat":"drink","title":"Turmeric Golden Milk (Light)","intro":"Warm low-fat milk simmered with turmeric, ginger, cinnamon and a pinch of black pepper, which helps the body absorb turmeric. It is a soothing bedtime drink that calms late-night cravings. It supplies protein and calcium. Sweeten with stevia if you need it.","kcal":100,"protein":6,"minutes":10,"ingredients":["1 cup low-fat milk","1/2 tsp turmeric","Pinch of black pepper","Pinch of cinnamon","1/2 inch ginger, grated","Pinch of nutmeg","Stevia (optional)"],"steps":["Pour milk into a small pan.","Add turmeric, pepper, cinnamon, ginger and nutmeg.","Simmer on low for 5 minutes, stirring.","Strain into a cup.","Sweeten lightly if needed and sip warm before bed."],"benefits":["Anti-inflammatory spices.","Protein and calcium.","Supports restful sleep.","Stops late-night snacking."]},{"id":"r111","cat":"sweet","title":"Lauki Ki Barfi","intro":"A soft, fudge-like barfi made with grated bottle gourd, milk and a little khoya-free milk powder, sweetened with dates or stevia. It satisfies sweet cravings with far fewer calories than regular mithai. Cardamom and pistachios make it festive. Perfect for Diwali on a diet.","kcal":110,"protein":4,"minutes":40,"ingredients":["2 cups grated lauki","1 cup low-fat milk","3 tbsp milk powder","4 dates, chopped (or stevia)","1/2 tsp cardamom powder","1 tsp ghee","1 tbsp chopped pistachios"],"steps":["Saute lauki in ghee for 5 minutes till the raw smell goes.","Add milk and cook stirring till it is absorbed.","Add dates and milk powder and cook till the mixture leaves the pan.","Stir in cardamom and spread on a greased plate.","Top with pistachios, cool and cut into squares."],"benefits":["About half the calories of regular","barfi.","Lauki adds fibre and volume.","No refined sugar.","Satisfies sweet cravings."]},{"id":"r112","cat":"sweet","title":"Date and Nut Ladoo","intro":"Soft, chewy energy balls made with dates, almonds, walnuts and flaxseed, with no added sugar at all. Dates provide natural sweetness and fibre, while nuts add healthy fats that keep you satisfied. One or two ladoos are perfect before a workout or when a sweet craving hits. They keep for two weeks in an airtight jar.","kcal":90,"protein":2,"minutes":15,"ingredients":["1 cup seedless dates","1/4 cup almonds","1/4 cup walnuts","1 tbsp flaxseeds","1 tbsp desiccated coconut","1/2 tsp cardamom powder","1 tsp ghee"],"steps":["Dry-roast almonds, walnuts and flaxseeds for 3 minutes and chop coarsely.","Blend dates into a sticky paste.","Warm ghee in a pan, add the date paste and cook 2 minutes.","Mix in nuts, flaxseed and cardamom and turn off the heat.","Grease palms, shape small ladoos and roll in coconut."],"benefits":["No refined sugar.","Instant natural energy.","Healthy fats and fibre.","Portion-controlled treat."]},{"id":"r113","cat":"sweet","title":"Ragi Halwa","intro":"A warm, glossy halwa made from roasted finger millet flour, jaggery and just a teaspoon of ghee. Ragi gives it a deep chocolatey colour and a nutty flavour. It is rich in calcium and fibre, so it satisfies without a sugar crash. Serve warm topped with sliced almonds.","kcal":140,"protein":3,"minutes":20,"ingredients":["1/4 cup ragi flour","2 tbsp jaggery powder","1 tsp ghee","1 cup water or low-fat milk","1/4 tsp cardamom powder","5 almonds, sliced"],"steps":["Roast ragi flour in ghee on low heat for 5 minutes until aromatic.","Warm water or milk and dissolve the jaggery in it.","Slowly pour the liquid into the ragi while stirring to avoid lumps.","Cook, stirring, until thick and glossy.","Add cardamom, garnish with almonds and serve warm."],"benefits":["High in calcium.","Jaggery instead of sugar.","Fibre-rich millet.","Satisfying small portion."]},{"id":"r114","cat":"sweet","title":"Oats Kheer","intro":"A creamy, comforting kheer made by simmering rolled oats in low-fat milk and sweetening with chopped dates. Saffron and cardamom give it the familiar festive aroma. Oats add fibre, making this dessert surprisingly filling. Enjoy warm or chilled.","kcal":160,"protein":7,"minutes":20,"ingredients":["3 tbsp rolled oats","2 cups low-fat milk","3 dates, finely chopped","1/4 tsp cardamom powder","Few saffron strands","1 tbsp chopped almonds and pistachios"],"steps":["Lightly roast oats in a dry pan for 2 minutes.","Bring milk to a boil and add the oats.","Simmer for 8-10 minutes, stirring often.","Add dates, cardamom and saffron and cook 2 minutes more.","Garnish with nuts and serve."],"benefits":["Fibre-rich dessert.","Protein and calcium from milk.","No refined sugar.","Keeps you full."]},{"id":"r115","cat":"sweet","title":"Shrikhand with Fruits","intro":"A thick, velvety Maharashtrian dessert of hung curd flavoured with saffron and cardamom, lightly sweetened and topped with fresh fruit. It is high in protein and probiotics. Using honey or stevia keeps the sugar low. Cool, creamy and very easy to make.","kcal":130,"protein":8,"minutes":15,"ingredients":["1 cup hung curd","1 tsp honey or stevia to taste","Few saffron strands soaked in 1 tbsp warm milk","1/4 tsp cardamom powder","1/2 cup chopped fruits (pomegranate, apple, mango)","1 tbsp chopped pistachios"],"steps":["Whisk hung curd until completely smooth.","Add sweetener, saffron milk and cardamom and mix well.","Chill for 30 minutes.","Spoon into bowls and top with fresh fruits.","Garnish with pistachios and serve."],"benefits":["High-protein dessert.","Low sugar.","Probiotic curd.","Refreshing and light."]},{"id":"r116","cat":"sweet","title":"Apple Cinnamon Baked Dessert","intro":"Apple slices tossed with cinnamon and a little honey, topped with an oat-and-nut crumble and baked until soft and bubbling. It tastes like apple pie without the buttery pastry. The apples are naturally sweet and full of fibre. Serve warm with a spoon of hung curd.","kcal":100,"protein":1,"minutes":25,"ingredients":["2 apples, thinly sliced","1 tsp cinnamon powder","1 tsp honey","2 tbsp rolled oats","1 tbsp chopped walnuts or almonds","1 tsp ghee, melted","Squeeze of lemon"],"steps":["Toss apple slices with cinnamon, honey and lemon.","Arrange in a small baking dish.","Mix oats, nuts and ghee and sprinkle over the apples.","Bake at 180 C for 20 minutes until golden.","Serve warm."],"benefits":["Fibre-rich and filling.","Cinnamon helps control sugar.","Naturally sweet.","Low calorie dessert."]},{"id":"r117","cat":"sweet","title":"Besan Ladoo (Jaggery)","intro":"The classic Diwali ladoo made lighter with less ghee and jaggery powder in place of sugar. Slow-roasting the besan brings out a deep, nutty aroma. Besan provides more protein than most sweets. One ladoo is enough to satisfy a craving.","kcal":120,"protein":3,"minutes":25,"ingredients":["1 cup besan","3 tbsp ghee","1/2 cup jaggery powder","1/2 tsp cardamom powder","2 tbsp chopped almonds and cashews"],"steps":["Heat ghee and add besan.","Roast on low heat, stirring constantly, for 15 minutes until golden and fragrant.","Cool until warm but not hot.","Mix in jaggery, cardamom and nuts.","Shape into small ladoos."],"benefits":["Plant protein from besan.","Less ghee.","Jaggery instead of white sugar.","Portion-controlled."]},{"id":"r118","cat":"sweet","title":"Makhana Kheer","intro":"Roasted fox nuts simmered in low-fat milk with dates, cardamom and saffron. Makhana is low in calories, high in protein and naturally gluten-free. Crushing half of it makes the kheer thick and creamy. A light dessert that is perfect during fasting days.","kcal":150,"protein":6,"minutes":20,"ingredients":["1 cup makhana","2 cups low-fat milk","3 dates, finely chopped","1/4 cup water","1/4 tsp cardamom powder","Few saffron strands","1 tbsp chopped almonds"],"steps":["Dry-roast makhana until crisp, then crush half of it coarsely.","Bring milk to a boil.","Add crushed and whole makhana and simmer 10 minutes.","Add dates, cardamom and saffron and cook 3 minutes more.","Garnish with almonds and serve warm or chilled."],"benefits":["Low calorie and gluten-free.","No refined sugar.","Protein and calcium.","Light and creamy."]},{"id":"r119","cat":"sweet","title":"Chia Mango Pudding","intro":"Chia seeds soaked overnight in cardamom-scented milk and layered with fresh mango puree. The seeds swell into a creamy pudding that is rich in fibre and omega-3 fats. Ripe mango gives all the sweetness you need. Make it the night before for a ready dessert.","kcal":150,"protein":5,"minutes":10,"ingredients":["2 tbsp chia seeds","1/2 cup low-fat milk","1/4 tsp cardamom powder","1/2 ripe mango","1 tsp honey (optional)","1 tbsp chopped pistachios"],"steps":["Stir chia seeds into milk with cardamom and honey.","Rest 10 minutes, stir again to break lumps.","Refrigerate 4 hours or overnight.","Blend half the mango into a puree and dice the rest.","Layer chia, mango puree and diced mango in a glass, top with pistachios."],"benefits":["Omega-3 fats and fibre.","Keeps you full.","Natural sweetness.","Make-ahead dessert."]},{"id":"r120","cat":"sweet","title":"Dates Coconut Rolls","intro":"No-cook rolls of date paste studded with nuts and coated in desiccated coconut, then chilled and sliced into rounds. They look like festive mithai yet contain no added sugar. Each slice gives quick energy and fibre. Ideal for gifting during festivals.","kcal":100,"protein":2,"minutes":15,"ingredients":["1 cup seedless dates","1/4 cup mixed nuts, chopped","2 tbsp desiccated coconut","1 tsp ghee","1/4 tsp cardamom powder","1 tsp poppy seeds (optional)"],"steps":["Blend dates into a smooth paste.","Cook the paste in ghee for 2-3 minutes until it comes together.","Mix in nuts and cardamom and let it cool slightly.","Shape into a log and roll in coconut and poppy seeds.","Chill 30 minutes and slice into rounds."],"benefits":["No added sugar.","Natural energy.","Healthy fats from nuts.","Easy festive treat."]},{"id":"r121","cat":"dip","title":"Green Chutney","intro":"A bright, fresh chutney of coriander, mint, green chillies, ginger and lemon. It adds big flavour to chillas, tikkas and sandwiches with almost no calories. Add a spoon of roasted chana for body. Keeps a week in the fridge.","kcal":15,"protein":1,"minutes":10,"ingredients":["1 cup coriander leaves","1/2 cup mint leaves","2 green chillies","1/2 inch ginger","1 tbsp roasted chana","Juice of 1 lemon","Pinch black salt","Salt and ice water"],"steps":["Wash herbs well.","Blend with chillies, ginger, chana and lemon.","Add ice water to keep it green.","Season with salt and black salt.","Store in a jar."],"benefits":["Almost zero calories.","Rich in antioxidants.","Aids digestion.","Replaces sauces and mayo."]},{"id":"r122","cat":"dip","title":"Hung Curd Dip","intro":"A thick, creamy dip of hung curd with grated garlic, fresh herbs, lemon and black pepper. It is a perfect substitute for mayonnaise in sandwiches, wraps and salads. Each spoon gives protein and probiotics with very few calories. Serve with carrot and cucumber sticks.","kcal":40,"protein":4,"minutes":10,"ingredients":["1 cup hung curd","1 garlic clove, grated","1 tbsp chopped dill, mint or coriander","1/2 tsp black pepper","1 tsp lemon juice","Pinch of oregano","Salt to taste"],"steps":["Hang curd in a muslin cloth for 3-4 hours to drain.","Whisk until smooth and creamy.","Add garlic, herbs, pepper, oregano and salt.","Stir in lemon juice.","Chill 15 minutes and serve with vegetable sticks."],"benefits":["High protein.","Replaces mayonnaise.","Probiotic.","Very low calorie."]},{"id":"r123","cat":"dip","title":"Tomato Garlic Chutney","intro":"A tangy, spicy South Indian chutney of roasted tomatoes, garlic and dry red chillies, finished with a mustard tempering. It has no sugar and only a few drops of oil. It pairs beautifully with dosa, idli and chilla. Keeps for four days in the fridge.","kcal":30,"protein":1,"minutes":15,"ingredients":["3 ripe tomatoes, chopped","6 garlic cloves","2 dry red chillies","1/2 tsp oil","1/2 tsp mustard seeds","6 curry leaves","Pinch of hing","Salt"],"steps":["Heat a few drops of oil and roast garlic and red chillies for a minute.","Add tomatoes and cook until soft and mushy.","Cool and blend with salt into a smooth chutney.","Heat remaining oil, crackle mustard seeds, curry leaves and hing.","Pour the tempering over the chutney."],"benefits":["Rich in lycopene.","No added sugar.","Very low calorie.","Big flavour for small portions."]},{"id":"r124","cat":"dip","title":"Roasted Chana Peanut Chutney","intro":"A creamy, protein-rich chutney made with roasted chana and a few peanuts instead of coconut. It has a lovely nutty taste and thick texture. Serve with idli, dosa or upma. A spoon of curd makes it extra smooth.","kcal":60,"protein":3,"minutes":10,"ingredients":["1/4 cup roasted chana dal","2 tbsp roasted peanuts","1 green chilli","1/2 inch ginger","2 tbsp curd","1/2 tsp mustard seeds and 6 curry leaves","Few drops oil","Salt"],"steps":["Blend chana, peanuts, chilli and ginger with a little water.","Add curd and salt and blend again until smooth.","Transfer to a bowl.","Heat oil, crackle mustard seeds and curry leaves.","Pour the tempering over and serve."],"benefits":["Plant protein.","Keeps you full.","Lower fat than coconut chutney.","Great with South Indian breakfasts."]},{"id":"r125","cat":"dip","title":"Beetroot Hummus","intro":"A vibrant pink dip of chickpeas blended with roasted beetroot, garlic, toasted sesame and lemon. It is rich in protein, fibre and antioxidants. Use it as a spread in wraps or as a dip for vegetables and roasted papad. It looks stunning on the table.","kcal":70,"protein":3,"minutes":15,"ingredients":["1 cup boiled chickpeas","1 small roasted beetroot","1 garlic clove","1 tbsp toasted sesame seeds","Juice of 1 lemon","1/2 tsp roasted cumin powder","1 tsp olive oil","Salt"],"steps":["Blend sesame seeds to a coarse powder.","Add chickpeas, beetroot, garlic, lemon, cumin and salt.","Blend until smooth, adding ice water as needed.","Transfer to a bowl and swirl the top.","Drizzle olive oil and serve."],"benefits":["Plant protein.","Rich in antioxidants.","High fibre.","Healthy fats from sesame."]}]"""

internal val RECIPE_JSON_PARTS: List<String> = listOf(PART_1, PART_2, PART_3)
